l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/810975-power-tiers-in-2e?p=811776#post811776\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ok, I just spent the last 20 minutes trying to find this damn Embed, where is it?</div> </div> </div> </div>Partitioned Memory, under Silent games in Chapter Three of the STG.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-19T08:21:51-08:00","id":811818,"title":"","content":"Thank you, that was really annoying me. <br /> <br /> But nonetheless, the ability to shield the truth from telepathic intrusion is redundant, because the Liars Tongue power says &quot;if the demon says \u201cthe sky is orange,\u201d <b>any</b> method of detecting truth or lies, <b>magical or otherwise,</b> reads that statement as\u201ctrue\u201d&quot;<br /> <br /> Reading a demon's mind is a method of discerning the truth. Therefore, it doesn't work.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-19T08:31:28-08:00","id":811828,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/810975-power-tiers-in-2e?p=811818#post811818\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But nonetheless, the ability to shield the truth from telepathic intrusion is redundant, because the Liars Tongue power says &quot;if the demon says \u201cthe sky is orange,\u201d <b>any</b> method of detecting truth or lies, <b>magical or otherwise,</b> reads that statement as\u201ctrue\u201d&quot;<br /> <br /> Reading a demon's mind is a method of discerning the truth. Therefore, it doesn't work.</div> </div> </div> </div>In the same sense that looking at the sky doesn't work, yes.<br /> <br /> &quot;If the demon says&quot; doesn't translate to &quot;if any means of extracting the information from the demon is used,&quot; or else Partitioned Memory, the sample near-field gadget from Flowers of Hell, and Mr. Spider's modus operandi from &quot;Retirement&quot; in the Interface are entirely nonsensical.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-19T08:33:27-08:00","id":811829,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/810975-power-tiers-in-2e?p=811800#post811800\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You can read a Demon's mind. And the thoughts you pick up can indeed be complete fabrications.</div> </div> </div> </div> Not without the Embed Satchel mentioned.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-19T08:44:30-08:00","id":811835,"title":"","content":"I wish there was a delete option.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2102,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","user":"MCN","date":". 01-19-2016, 11:53 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-19T08:50:31-08:00","id":811839,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/810975-power-tiers-in-2e?p=811788#post811788\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This. Sure, you overlooked Sin-Eaters, Mummies, and hunters; but you demonstrated that the principle is sound.</div> </div> </div> </div> Oh, I didn't overlook them. There's no 2e equivalent for them yet, so I don't consider them worth discussion on the matter yet. I don't like comparing 1e to 2e. Totally different games.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> This is what I meant about there being at least as many challenges as types, with each type being best at <i>something</i> important; and a list of what each supernatural type is good at is <i>far</i> more valuable than an attempt to set up an overall hierarchy of best to worst. </div> </div> </div> Exactly. Play to your strengths, you're better off than someone who doesn't.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-19T08:50:42-08:00","id":811840,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PenDragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/810975-power-tiers-in-2e?p=811634#post811634\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Seconding Dataweaver yet again.<br /> <br /> Further more you are going to run into complications vis-a-vis the theoretical ideal and the practical example of a splat. Mages, for instance, are all but guaranteed to top nearly every category. This will come as no surprise to anyone who knows Mage well, it's a game where <u>power</u> is a key theme, and the general response to &quot;Can a Mage do that?&quot; is &quot;Yes, eleven different ways&quot;. Of course, in practical application this is miles from the truth, a real character won't have access to all Arcana, unfailing situational comprehension or a pure utilitarian personality, and that's not accounting for time, scenario and the player simply dropping the ball. But the theoretical Mage-Splat Mage does, and that's what the Tier list will reflect.<br /> <br /> Similarly, Vampires are likely to rank low in many categories where, in the context of a story, they would probably shine. Combat is a good example, Vampires pale in comparison to Werewolves in white room battles. We had a thread on it, it's not a good matchup...in the white room. Largely because the white room utterly neglects all the social manipulation, preparation, and sheer get-out-of-dodge potential the kindred possess. Throw in context to manipulate and suddenly Vampires will astonish you with their out of the box problem solving. Of course that's true for all splats (especially Demon, the unchained are ungodly good at out of the box problem solving), but that really only makes the tier problem worse.<br /> <br /> Never the less, if we are to engage in tier making I shall propose a few: <ol class=\"decimal\"><li>Which splats are best at getting elected president?</li> <li>Which splats are best at sleeping?</li> <li>Which splats are best at cleaning up the streets? (I mean literally cleaning them of dirt and litter, not crime. Ignore crime. Except littering, assuming that's a crime where you live.)</li> <li>Which splats are best at eating someone's Grandmother, putting on her cloths, and impersonating her when her granddaughter comes to visit?</li> </ol></div> </div> </div> </div>2. Deathless because well....they're mummies after all.<br /> <br /> On another note. I have found myself somewhat surprised at how the conventions of Mummy:the Curse have help make the concept of power tiers less of a thing for me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-19T08:56:55-08:00","id":811844,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/810975-power-tiers-in-2e?p=811727#post811727\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> One, this is an opinion, not fact. Two, it depends on edition, blanket statements are meaningless. Three, it doesn't matter if it doesn't work. What matters is that ranking power and ability is an innate part of D&amp;D. Saying otherwise is just being in denial.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well first and foremost, CR isn't a measurement of a player characters power to begin with, it's a measurement of monster threat level calculated by arbitrarily giving various traits a numerical value then adding them up and assigning them to level brackets based of the final number. And if we're counting something like <i>that</i> then the CofD <i>also</i> has something similar with the ranking system for the various Ephemerals. If anything, I'd say that <i>level</i> itself is the closest thing you're going to get to a true measurement of player character power, and if we're counting <i>that</i> then total experience in CofD mirrors that well enough. The quick reference sheets in the various splat books even list nice little names for them. For Demon it's Established Presence at 5, Respected Veteran at 10 and so on.<br /> <br /> And you've still yet to acknowledge that <i>none of that matters regardless</i>. Tier lists aren't based on CR, and as milo v3 has pointed out, not even based purely off of combat ability. IIRC, if we we're only talking about damage dealt per round, and the ability to make the enemy go splat, Barbarians were one of the best in the game at doing that. And they were only like, what? Tier 3, Tier 4?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/810975-power-tiers-in-2e?p=811839#post811839\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Exactly. Play to your strengths, you're better off than someone who doesn't.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree, but how <i>much</i> better, comparatively? And how do various splats handle not being in their specialized element, and which ones adapt better to what? This is part of what Tier lists are there to measure.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2309,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2309-ashenrogue","user":"Ashenrogue","date":". 01-19-2016, 12:04 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2309-ashenrogue","name":"Ashenrogue","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1388"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-19T09:07:21-08:00","id":811852,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ashenrogue</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/810975-power-tiers-in-2e?p=811844#post811844\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I agree, but how <i>much</i> better, comparatively? And how do various splats handle not being in their specialized element, and which ones adapt better to what? This is part of what Tier lists are there to measure.</div> </div> </div> </div>Indeed. Broadly speaking, and <u>all else being equal</u>, a Vampire or Demon is better in the Social arena then a Promethean, for instance. And the average Promethean is just more rugged and survivable than, say, your average Changeling.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-19T09:11:48-08:00","id":811855,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/810975-power-tiers-in-2e?p=811603#post811603\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Getting back on topic: I don't have any proof of this, but I suspect that trying to rank the supernatural types based on how well they cope with a particular type of challenge will end up with a list of challenges at least as long as the list of supernatural types, with each type taking first place in at least one of the challenge rankings.<br /> <br /> Also keep in mind that a given challenge ranking might end up with a <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Partially_ordered_set\" target=\"_blank\">partial order</a> due to the inability to find a basis for comparison between two types that approach the challenge in fundamentally different ways. Indeed, I suspect that this will prove to be the rule rather than the exception. You might not even be able to get a clear \u201cbest\u201d (or \u201cworst\u201d), for that matter.</div> </div> </div> </div>There are only like six types of character in 2e (Vampires, Werewolves, Demons, Beasts, Mortal, Mortal+), so there probably will be about that categories. This really isn't as complicated an issue as it's being made out to be.<br /> <br /> Try and prove your side with just one category. The category is: get an individual to do something for you that they do not inherently want to do. What are each splat's options? How are they so different that they can not be compared?<br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1157-soulgambit","name":"SoulGambit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"912"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-19T09:28:28-08:00","id":811866,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SoulGambit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/810975-power-tiers-in-2e?p=811855#post811855\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Try and prove your side with just one category. The category is: get an individual to do something for you that they do not inherently want to do. What are each splat's options? How are they so different that they can not be compared?</div> </div> </div> </div> Not enough details. Werewolves Cunning Dominance gift allows short term Perfect Impression for something that has to be done in the immediate. The wolves have a strong advantage for getting someone outside to smoke a little, but there would need to be a different approach for changing a lawmaker's mind about zoning through persuasion. Demons can manipulate connections and desires, and opening Doors, but I'm fairly sure that they have no way of directly hacking Impressions like others can, and they have limited ability to deal with anything resembling a spotlight. Attention is deadly. Is the vampire's daylight restrictions going to be an issue? Are we talking about dealing with supernaturals or mundanes here, because that's a rather important question when it comes to Beasts.<br /> <br /> And so on. There's a lot of information you're not providing here that makes all the difference in the world.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2102,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","user":"MCN","date":". 01-19-2016, 12:34 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-19T09:38:58-08:00","id":811874,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/810975-power-tiers-in-2e?p=811866#post811866\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Not enough details. Werewolves Cunning Dominance gift allows short term Perfect Impression for something that has to be done in the immediate. The wolves have a strong advantage for getting someone outside to smoke a little, but there would need to be a different approach for changing a lawmaker's mind about zoning through persuasion. Demons can manipulate connections and desires, and opening Doors, but I'm fairly sure that they have no way of directly hacking Impressions like others can, and they have limited ability to deal with anything resembling a spotlight. Attention is deadly. Is the vampire's daylight restrictions going to be an issue? Are we talking about dealing with supernaturals or mundanes here, because that's a rather important question when it comes to Beasts.<br /> <br /> And so on. There's a lot of information you're not providing here that makes all the difference in the world.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd assume we'd take all of these things into consideration, as you have, and list how they might do so the easiest and what shortcomings said method has and how they would then overcome said shortcoming. So you're off to a pretty good start.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2309-ashenrogue","name":"Ashenrogue","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1388"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-19T09:50:07-08:00","id":811881,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ashenrogue</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/810975-power-tiers-in-2e?p=811874#post811874\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd assume we'd take all of these things into consideration, as you have, and list how they might do so the easiest and what shortcomings said method has and how they would then overcome said shortcoming. So you're off to a pretty good start.</div> </div> </div> </div> But that's just it. There's too much. You can't rate &quot;Well, the mayor goes golfing at noon, and a vampire can't go, but he also surrounds himself with the most banal disbelievers in the world, so magic is a no go, but werewolf pheramones are highly rated.&quot; Its just too situational.<br /> <br /> And that's exactly the point. There's just too many variables to make a good generality. Like Dataweaver said, you'd have to make a list of a million scenarios, then try to guess on all of them. Worse, it also doesn't take into account things like how different people approach things. Irraka, Cahalisth, and Elodoth approach social things from three different angles, as do the vampire clans, and mage Paths (Acanthus using Fate/Time have different methods than Mastigos or the more primal Thyrsus, or even the Moros with ghosts or monetary bribes).<br /> <br /> And what if your ST favors one kind of scenario over others? Nothing says all scenarios are equally distributed over every table. And what about the type of story? Is a werewolf really going to be interested in high level politics instead of their territory? What about Orders and Tribes and other social groupings? Simply asking the local elder person and favor trading? Are we assumign that we'd have a &quot;twice-blessed&quot; troupe, and access to one of every x- and y-axis? Does it count if a vampire teaches a ghoul Dominate 2 and Obfuscate 1, and sends them everywhere? What about a goetic summoner who effectively brainwashes people like the True Fae do?<br /> <br /> Its not a good start, because all it does in reveal the sheer about of variance you have to take into account. If you want to create a list, you will need to start from the same base. however, its impossible to create the same base for everyone that doesn't show at least SOME bias, which skews results. An attempt to create a white-room-social-maneuevering is just as worthless as a white room combat. If not more so.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2102,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","user":"MCN","date":". 01-19-2016, 12:54 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-19T09:53:05-08:00","id":811888,"title":"","content":"Also, the werewolf's pack totem might know Implant Mission.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-19T09:58:32-08:00","id":811892,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/810975-power-tiers-in-2e?p=811881#post811881\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> But that's just it. There's too much. You can't rate &quot;Well, the mayor goes golfing at noon, and a vampire can't go, but he also surrounds himself with the most banal disbelievers in the world, so magic is a no go, but werewolf pheramones are highly rated.&quot; Its just too situational.<br /> <br /> And that's exactly the point. There's just too many variables to make a good generality. Like Dataweaver said, you'd have to make a list of a million scenarios, then try to guess on all of them. Worse, it also doesn't take into account things like how different people approach things. Irraka, Cahalisth, and Elodoth approach social things from three different angles, as do the vampire clans, and mage Paths (Acanthus using Fate/Time have different methods than Mastigos or the more primal Thyrsus, or even the Moros with ghosts or monetary bribes).<br /> <br /> And what if your ST favors one kind of scenario over others? Nothing says all scenarios are equally distributed over every table. And what about the type of story? Is a werewolf really going to be interested in high level politics instead of their territory? What about Orders and Tribes and other social groupings? Simply asking the local elder person and favor trading? Are we assumign that we'd have a &quot;twice-blessed&quot; troupe, and access to one of every x- and y-axis? Does it count if a vampire teaches a ghoul Dominate 2 and Obfuscate 1, and sends them everywhere? What about a goetic summoner who effectively brainwashes people like the True Fae do?<br /> <br /> Its not a good start, because all it does in reveal the sheer about of variance you have to take into account. If you want to create a list, you will need to start from the same base. however, its impossible to create the same base for everyone that doesn't show at least SOME bias, which skews results. An attempt to create a white-room-social-maneuevering is just as worthless as a white room combat. If not more so.</div> </div> </div> </div>You're really overthinking this. Tier lists are based off of pretty broad strokes, and you aren't really expected to come up with the whole thing yourself. Tier lists have always been more of a community effort. The variables will be taken into account, don't worry yourself trying to do it all yourself. It'll work itself out, it always does.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2309-ashenrogue","name":"Ashenrogue","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1388"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-19T10:21:00-08:00","id":811918,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ashenrogue</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/810975-power-tiers-in-2e?p=811892#post811892\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You're really overthinking this. Tier lists are based off of pretty broad strokes, and you aren't really expected to come up with the whole thing yourself. Tier lists have always been more of a community effort. The variables will be taken into account, don't worry yourself trying to do it all yourself. It'll work itself out, it always does.</div> </div> </div> </div>Traditionally Tier lists are a combination of aggregate data, theory craft and opinion. This works for games like Street Fighter, Starcraft and Call of Duty because of their repetition, sheer player base and the ease by which data (and opinion) is gathered. The same stands, to a lesser extent, for D&amp;D. Where at the very least all the characters are expected to tackle the same challenges in roughly the same manner.<br /> <br /> But CofD? Broad strokes, sure, but strokes look different depending on the canvas. We have no repeatable scenarios, everyone's story is different, with different priorities and different storytellers run the splats in radically different ways. I just cannot see how it is possible, or remotely productive, to create tier lists. Hell, even if we had all the necessary factors, tier lists are so frequently upset, debated and revised as to render them dubious even in the most statistically rigorous environment.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <b>Mod Voice is <u><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">RED</span></u>*</b><br /> <i>*All other colors should be read aloud in the voice of Don Knotts</i><b>.</b> <hr /><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/18519-pendragon-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">Hacks and House Rules Hub Thread</a></b><br /> <br /> <b>CofD Hacks By Splat: <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/13vBLaS5Ua1Ez-cVyK6uFa4ssvYeIIZpoA5GQTXytfcA/edit\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Vampire</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1sqltG7X-C_MdEe00PtVOZmki8V_K1M1FpQtLwTvb2jg/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#006400\">Werewolf</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1bpr1EjQ4RfZ5dz-tXmJJ93P2f_l7fUIUwpPLWs9Z-SI/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800080\">Mage</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1vKpSTktCUuUaqxXncG4txQPtvPclzXlFZEEX7tbrTSg/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Mummy</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Spynbcs_VgCDHdooKWXobZNe6C9CMjONeRTlvXIq9fI/edit?usp=drive_web\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Demon</span></a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/148-pendragon","name":"PenDragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar148_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1657"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-19T10:21:08-08:00","id":811919,"title":"","content":"There's not much to overthink. It just doesn't work. It just doesn't work without more specifics. And those specifics will vary between tables and playing styles. Fine, you do it. I'm tired of arguing that it can't be done due to the game's subjective nature. I've provided reasoning and rationale why it doesn't work. And you know, I'm a huge fan of proof. <br /> <br /> Make your list. Start right here and now. Rate vamps, demons, wolves, mortals, and Beasts. Do it anyway you want. If you can give one that's halfway accurate and not showing obvious bias, I'll conceed on the matter. Prove me wrong.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-19T10:29:38-08:00","id":811923,"title":"","content":"The best use of Tiers as a useful concept to players and Storytellers I've seen was one about 1e New World of Darkness splats from a while back on rpg.net. The basic idea of the thread was a grouping roughly under an idea of raw mechanical power as a way of helping guide people when it came to potential cross overs. The idea being as long as you were within one tier up or down in a cross over you were in a general sense ok without the sheer mechanical prowess of a particular splat running roughshod over another. Where as if you got into the territory of 2 or more tiers of difference you were going to start to run into issues of player agency.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-19T10:41:25-08:00","id":811931,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PenDragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/810975-power-tiers-in-2e?p=811918#post811918\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Traditionally Tier lists are a combination of aggregate data, theory craft and opinion. This works for games like Street Fighter, Starcraft and Call of Duty because of their repetition, sheer player base and the ease by which data (and opinion) is gathered. The same stands, to a lesser extent, for D&amp;D. Where at the very least all the characters are expected to tackle the same challenges in roughly the same manner.<br /> <br /> But CofD? Broad strokes, sure, but strokes look different depending on the canvas. We have no repeatable scenarios, everyone's story is different, with different priorities and different storytellers run the splats in radically different ways. I just cannot see how it is possible, or remotely productive, to create tier lists. Hell, even if we had all the necessary factors, tier lists are so frequently upset, debated and revised as to render them dubious even in the most statistically rigorous environment.</div> </div> </div> </div>Again, I really feel like you're exaggerating how difficult this really is. Like by several magnitudes. While I'd agree that D&amp;D is generally going to feature more combat on average, it isn't really going to be that much different from that. Sure, there are pre-made adventures for D&amp;D, but I wouldn't say that that makes up the bulk of games played. So even there you can say everyones story is different, with different priorities, and different DMs... Actually, I'm not even quite sure what you meant here. Are you talking about homebrew? Using different rules? Having different character goals? All of these things are done quite frequently even there. So long story short, it really shouldn't be anymore difficult to create tier lists for this than it would for that, barring disparity in fan population.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2309-ashenrogue","name":"Ashenrogue","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1388"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-19T11:52:12-08:00","id":811987,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/810975-power-tiers-in-2e?p=811818#post811818\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thank you, that was really annoying me.<br /> <br /> But nonetheless, the ability to shield the truth from telepathic intrusion is redundant, because the Liars Tongue power says &quot;if the demon says \u201cthe sky is orange,\u201d <b>any</b> method of detecting truth or lies, <b>magical or otherwise,</b> reads that statement as\u201ctrue\u201d&quot;<br /> <br /> Reading a demon's mind is a method of discerning the truth. Therefore, it doesn't work.</div> </div> </div> </div>My interpretation of that rule has always been that a spell asking &quot;Is the demon correct/being truthful (pick your preferred version) when he says the sky is orange&quot; would return &quot;Yes/True&quot;, while a spell asking &quot;Is the sky orange&quot; would return &quot;No, it's blue.&quot;<br /> <br /> Methods of verification <i>work</i>, but they have to be completely independent of whether or not the demon is lying about it. In this situation, the Mind Arcanum would be useless, for example, while Forces (for determining wavelengths directly) would give you the correct answer.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1909-juhn","name":"Juhn","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"302"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-19T12:08:15-08:00","id":811998,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ashenrogue</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/810975-power-tiers-in-2e?p=811931#post811931\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Again, I really feel like you're exaggerating how difficult this really is. Like by several magnitudes. While I'd agree that D&amp;D is generally going to feature more combat on average, it isn't really going to be that much different from that. Sure, there are pre-made adventures for D&amp;D, but I wouldn't say that that makes up the bulk of games played. So even there you can say everyones story is different, with different priorities, and different DMs... Actually, I'm not even quite sure what you meant here. Are you talking about homebrew? Using different rules? Having different character goals? All of these things are done quite frequently even there. So long story short, it really shouldn't be anymore difficult to create tier lists for this than it would for that, barring disparity in fan population.</div> </div> </div> </div>Difficult? No. I'm saying it's flat out impossible. I mean, sure you <b>can </b>make a tier list, and maybe it will be valuable to a handful of people. But it won't mean anything, not practically. Making a tier list for CofD is kinda like trying to tier True Blood, The X-Files, Supernatural, The Invisibles, and Once Upon A Time together.<br /> <br /> What metric do we even use? Versatility? Mages are gonna rock the house there. Combat? That almost certainly means white rooms, and grotesque Werewolf overkill. Will the tier list account for different experience levels? Integrity-stat degeneration? Will it address different game types? Because a vampiric politics setting is gonna have a mighty different tier list than an on-the-run Demonic spy-thriller.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <b>Mod Voice is <u><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">RED</span></u>*</b><br /> <i>*All other colors should be read aloud in the voice of Don Knotts</i><b>.</b> <hr /><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/18519-pendragon-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">Hacks and House Rules Hub Thread</a></b><br /> <br /> <b>CofD Hacks By Splat: <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/13vBLaS5Ua1Ez-cVyK6uFa4ssvYeIIZpoA5GQTXytfcA/edit\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Vampire</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1sqltG7X-C_MdEe00PtVOZmki8V_K1M1FpQtLwTvb2jg/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#006400\">Werewolf</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1bpr1EjQ4RfZ5dz-tXmJJ93P2f_l7fUIUwpPLWs9Z-SI/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800080\">Mage</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1vKpSTktCUuUaqxXncG4txQPtvPclzXlFZEEX7tbrTSg/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Mummy</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Spynbcs_VgCDHdooKWXobZNe6C9CMjONeRTlvXIq9fI/edit?usp=drive_web\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Demon</span></a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/148-pendragon","name":"PenDragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar148_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1657"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-19T12:19:06-08:00","id":812007,"title":"","content":"Things like Challenge Ratings,etc tend to get brought up when it comes to D&amp;D because of it's origins with Chainmail and tactical miniature games. Obviously the game has changed over the years but it's also when it tends to be a thing for D&amp;D more so than other games.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-19T13:52:55-08:00","id":812085,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PenDragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/810975-power-tiers-in-2e?p=811998#post811998\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Difficult? No. I'm saying it's flat out impossible. I mean, sure you <b>can </b>make a tier list, and maybe it will be valuable to a handful of people. But it won't mean anything, not practically. Making a tier list for CofD is kinda like trying to tier True Blood, The X-Files, Supernatural, The Invisibles, and Once Upon A Time together.<br /> <br /> What metric do we even use? Versatility? Mages are gonna rock the house there. Combat? That almost certainly means white rooms, and grotesque Werewolf overkill. Will the tier list account for different experience levels? Integrity-stat degeneration? Will it address different game types? Because a vampiric politics setting is gonna have a mighty different tier list than an on-the-run Demonic spy-thriller.</div> </div> </div> </div>Like all tier lists you have to define the metric you're using. <i>This isn't that complicated.</i> Have you seen the 3.5 Tier list?<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Tier 1: Capable of doing absolutely everything, often better than classes that specialize in that thing. Often capable of solving encounters with a single mechanical ability and little thought from the player. Has world changing powers at high levels. These guys, if played well, can break a campaign and can be very hard to challenge without extreme DM fiat, especially if Tier 3s and below are in the party.<br /> <br /> Tier 2: Has as much raw power as the Tier 1 classes, but can't pull off nearly as many tricks, and while the class itself is capable of anything, no one build can actually do nearly as much as the Tier 1 classes. Still potentially campaign smashers by using the right abilities, but at the same time are more predictable and can't always have the right tool for the job. If the Tier 1 classes are countries with 10,000 nuclear weapons in their arsenal, these guys are countries with 10 nukes. Still dangerous and world shattering, but not in quite so many ways. Note that the Tier 2 classes are often less flexible than Tier 3 classes... it's just that their incredible potential power overwhelms their lack in flexibility.<br /> <br /> Tier 3: Capable of doing one thing quite well, while still being useful when that one thing is inappropriate, or capable of doing all things, but not as well as classes that specialize in that area. Occasionally has a mechanical ability that can solve an encounter, but this is relatively rare and easy to deal with. Challenging such a character takes some thought from the DM, but isn't too difficult. Will outshine any Tier 5s in the party much of the time.<br /> <br /> Tier 4: Capable of doing one thing quite well, but often useless when encounters require other areas of expertise, or capable of doing many things to a reasonable degree of competance without truly shining. Rarely has any abilities that can outright handle an encounter unless that encounter plays directly to the class's main strength. DMs may sometimes need to work to make sure Tier 4s can contribue to an encounter, as their abilities may sometimes leave them useless. Won't outshine anyone except Tier 6s except in specific circumstances that play to their strengths. Cannot compete effectively with Tier 1s that are played well.<br /> <br /> Tier 5: Capable of doing only one thing, and not necessarily all that well, or so unfocused that they have trouble mastering anything, and in many types of encounters the character cannot contribute. In some cases, can do one thing very well, but that one thing is very often not needed. Has trouble shining in any encounter unless the rest of the party is weak in that situation and the encounter matches their strengths. DMs may have to work to avoid the player feeling that their character is worthless unless the entire party is Tier 4 and below. Characters in this tier will often feel like one trick ponies if they do well, or just feel like they have no tricks at all if they build the class poorly.<br /> <br /> Tier 6: Not even capable of shining in their own area of expertise. DMs will need to work hard to make encounters that this sort of character can contribute in with their mechanical abilities. Will often feel worthless unless the character is seriously powergamed beyond belief, and even then won't be terribly impressive. Needs to fight enemies of lower than normal CR. Class is often completely unsynergized or with almost no abilities of merit. Avoid allowing PCs to play these characters. </div> </div> </div></div></div> </div> </div><br /> Now to be fair, the bottom tiers are almost certainly not going to apply. Even taking into account Minor Templates and base mortals I don't think anything is likely to ever hit lower than Tier 4, probably even Tier 3. This game simply lacks the downward power variance of 3.5, which is why a dedicated tier list for this game should probably have more focused tiers than 3.5 did due to having less power variation. So no, it isn't impossible. Hell, while not ideal, even this could work. Looking up the 5e Tier list, they've not got anything below Tier 3, so it isn't like knocking off a couple of tiers or a tighter power variation somehow makes this impossible.<br /> <br /> Those games have social situations with just as many potential variables as this one and they managed to pull it off, so I don't want to hear about it being somehow impossible here. You may not want to spend the effort in coming up with it, which is fine, and is your choice, but don't try to pretend it just can't be done.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2309,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2309-ashenrogue","user":"Ashenrogue","date":". 01-19-2016, 05:00 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2309-ashenrogue","name":"Ashenrogue","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1388"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-19T14:44:44-08:00","id":812133,"title":"","content":"The D&amp;D tier list, which I'm very familiar with, is built on the assumption that all the characters will form a party, and run through combat heavy, D&amp;D style encounters. And there's nothing wrong with that, that's how D&amp;D is expected to be played. Mind you, I've played games with Wizards who were considerably worse than the party Fighter, and Rogues who were on par with the average sorcerer. But if what you're looking for is a Tier list that ranks the splats based on the assumption that they are all collectively working as a party to defeat Storyteller placed obstacles, I can probably gander a decent one:<br /> <br /> <b>I'm gonna put this in spoilers, so people read my post before they assume I've suddenly flipped to the idea of Tiers.</b><br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <b>Tier 1 (The 'Demigod' Tier)</b>: <i>Mages/Demons</i> - Both Mages and Demons have supreme flexibility, Mages through Creative Thaumaturgy, and Demons through their more open ended Embeds and Exploits (Looking at you <i>Shift Consequence</i> &amp; <i>The Word</i>). More importantly both splats can solve challenges without ever going near them, and are difficult to find even if you are another Mage/Demon. Both have the potential to invite cosmic superpowers onto the field that other splats would struggle to contend with, and have Masquerade effects (Quiessence &amp; Spoofing) that passively hide them from the public eye.<br /> <br /> <b>Tier 2 (The 'Oops, Bye' Tier)</b>: <i>Changelings/Sin-Eaters/Beasts</i> - All three splats are nearly invisible, indistinguishable from normal humans until placed under considerable magical scrutiny. Each is also equipped with a host of fantastic template traits, and few self control issues. Most importantly, while not as versatile as Mages and Demons, all three are equipped with powerful Get Out of Jail Free effects, and have mostly free reign with their supernatural powers.<br /> <br /> <b>Tier 3 (The 'You Won't Like Me When I'm Angry' Tier)</b>: <i>Werewolves/Mummies </i>- Basically the same as Tier 2, save that these splats come with stupendous drawbacks (Kuruth &amp; Descent) that constantly threaten to force the character into dangerous situations. While both lack run-away buttons on the level of Tier 2 (from a utilitarian perspective Mummies lose more from dying than a Sin-Eater does), they are extremely durable when pressed and capable of incredible burst power. Both Werewolves and Mummies also assume the presence of copious NPC allies, which in a normal game is certainly a boon, but in a tier list measuring their individual power among a group of supernaturals is mostly a setback.<br /> <br /> <b>Tier 4 (The 'If It Weren't For All These Banes' Tier)</b>: <i>Vampires/Prometheans</i> - Both splats, while possessed of formidable supernatural abilities, suffer from drawbacks so extreme as to dramatically limit their utility (again, in an objective based cohesive party game). Vampires suffer during the day, and Prometheans suffer in crowds. Both also labor under the 'anger issues' clause of Tier 3, but without the astonishing mechanical overdrive that makes Kuruth so powerful.<br /> <br /> I won't bother with the many mini splats (though I'd probably put the Purified up in Tier 2, with the other splats good at taking multiple tries to solve a problem), or Hunters (who would probably kick Vampires and Prometheans down to Tier 5, thanks to not suffering terrible banes).<br /> <br /> There. IMO that's a pretty convincing D&amp;D style Tier list, and one I'd argue is largely accurate...assuming everyone is playing a utilitarian problem solving machine and not an actual human being with hopes, fears and interests.<br /> </div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <b>Mod Voice is <u><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">RED</span></u>*</b><br /> <i>*All other colors should be read aloud in the voice of Don Knotts</i><b>.</b> <hr /><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/18519-pendragon-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">Hacks and House Rules Hub Thread</a></b><br /> <br /> <b>CofD Hacks By Splat: <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/13vBLaS5Ua1Ez-cVyK6uFa4ssvYeIIZpoA5GQTXytfcA/edit\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Vampire</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1sqltG7X-C_MdEe00PtVOZmki8V_K1M1FpQtLwTvb2jg/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#006400\">Werewolf</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1bpr1EjQ4RfZ5dz-tXmJJ93P2f_l7fUIUwpPLWs9Z-SI/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800080\">Mage</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1vKpSTktCUuUaqxXncG4txQPtvPclzXlFZEEX7tbrTSg/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Mummy</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Spynbcs_VgCDHdooKWXobZNe6C9CMjONeRTlvXIq9fI/edit?usp=drive_web\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Demon</span></a></b>","edited":{"userid":148,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/148-pendragon","user":"PenDragon","date":". 01-19-2016, 05:47 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/148-pendragon","name":"PenDragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar148_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1657"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-19T14:56:01-08:00","id":812143,"title":"","content":"Thanks for the tiers, PenDragon. Their usefulness doesn't lie in a white room reductionist &quot;my fave is better than your fave&quot; approach, but as a general Storyteller guide when doing crossovers. Not even as a dealbreaker (&quot;oh no, I can't have this mage and this vampire on the same game!&quot;), but as a cautionary mechanism (&quot;I probably want to pay additional attention to the vampire to make sure he doesn't feel left out, and give him something useful he can do every session, even if I do let the Mage play Batman and solve everything from her Sanctum.&quot;).<br /> <br /> IMO that's the value of a tier list. It's easy to think of challenges and stories for same-splat chronicles. However, there are some pitfalls involving crossovers that aren't immediately apparent.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/872434-shadow-knight-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10056-shadowknight1224","name":"ShadowKnight1224","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"975"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-19T15:02:19-08:00","id":812151,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ShadowKnight1224</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/810975-power-tiers-in-2e?p=812143#post812143\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thanks for the tiers, PenDragon. Their usefulness doesn't lie in a white room reductionist &quot;my fave is better than your fave&quot; approach, but as a general Storyteller guide when doing crossovers. Not even as a dealbreaker (&quot;oh no, I can't have this mage and this vampire on the same game!&quot;), but as a cautionary mechanism (&quot;I probably want to pay additional attention to the vampire to make sure he doesn't feel left out, and give him something useful he can do every session, even if I do let the Mage play Batman and solve everything from her Sanctum.&quot;).<br /> <br /> IMO that's the value of a tier list. It's easy to think of challenges and stories for same-splat chronicles. However, there are some pitfalls involving crossovers that aren't immediately apparent.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'll agree with you that Tier lists tend to highlight this issue (and blow it wildly out of proportion), but frankly that is something a Storyteller should already be doing. A socialite Carthian is going to be just as out of place in a game of cruac wielding crones as he is in a game of Mystagogue lore divers. Sure the exact nature of the issue will be slightly different, but no less prominent.<br /> <br /> For crossover one would be far better served by a guide to the themes, expertise and restrictions of each splat (ala MCN's post on <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/810975-power-tiers-in-2e?p=811727#post811727\">page 4</a>) than a list rating them on a 1 - X scale.<br /> <br /> <b>Edit: </b>If I were constructing a tiering of splat based on ability to ruin everyone's fun it'd probably look like:<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <b>Tier 1: Beast</b> - They are literally encouraged to fuck with other splats, driving them towards the same bestial depravity Beasts themselves glorify. How this was ever deemed the crossover splat I'll never know. This falls to Tier 6 if the player plays a particularly bland, unoffensive beast.<br /> <br /> <b>Tier 2: Werewolf/Promethean</b> - One bad Kuruth or a little too much Disquiet can collapse into total, involuntary party murder. Otherwise great team players, but it just takes one bad roll.<br /> <br /> <b>Tier 3: Mage/Demon</b> - Both can run rampant, but that's more or less a player problem. And unlike Beasts they aren't encouraged to fuck over their fellows. True they have the potential to invoke cosmic horrors, but those risks can be consciously mitigated and the antagonists are storyteller controlled.<br /> <br /> <b>Tier 4: Mummy</b> - Mummies aren't equipped with the same accidental gamesplosian powers as other splats, but their extremely objective oriented nature and bizarre powerstat can make them difficult to integrate and shift the focus of the game towards their own descent.<br /> <br /> <b>Tier 5: Vampire/Changeling/Sin-Eater</b> - All three can upend the game, but unlike Beasts they are not encouraged to, and unlike Tier 2-3 it's unlikely to trigger on them involuntarily (Frenzy maybe, but that's easier to weather without everyone dying).<br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <b>Edit #2</b>: And if I were making a tiering for which splats can be the best crossover buddies...<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <b>Tier 1: Mage/Demon </b>- The same flexibility that makes them the utilitarian power gamer's best friend, also shines in the hand of the party friendly player. Used to supplement their allies, instead of invalidating them, Mages &amp; Demons can shower their friends with buffs, merits, and tools to ease their way through life.<br /> <br /> <b>Tier 2: Werewolf/Mummy </b>- Who doesn't like a friend who also comes with a host of allies/cultists, protected territory/tomb and neigh invulnerable meat shield. They can also protect you from Spirits and Ghosts respectively, which is nice.<br /> <br /> <b>Tier 3: Changelings/Beasts </b>- Pledges, family dinner, dice boons and social smoothing. What's not to like. They can also sneak you out of a tight corner, albeit into a no less dangerous corner (the hedge/their lair).<br /> <br /> <b>Tier 4: Vampires/Sin-Eaters </b>- Vampires could easily be tier 2, with a cozy haven and loyal bodyguards. Same with Sin-Eaters and their ghastly (meant here as a complement) krewe. But as neither are base assumptions of the splat, they sit down here.<br /> <br /> <b>Tier 5: Prometheans</b> - Prometheans are shitty friends. They make your house smell and your friends avoid you. They are probably stealing from you as well, and talking behind your back. Why do you even talk to them? Hell, why do you suffer them to live? Burn them. BUUUUUUURN!!!!!<br /> </div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <b>Mod Voice is <u><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">RED</span></u>*</b><br /> <i>*All other colors should be read aloud in the voice of Don Knotts</i><b>.</b> <hr /><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/18519-pendragon-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">Hacks and House Rules Hub Thread</a></b><br /> <br /> <b>CofD Hacks By Splat: <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/13vBLaS5Ua1Ez-cVyK6uFa4ssvYeIIZpoA5GQTXytfcA/edit\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Vampire</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1sqltG7X-C_MdEe00PtVOZmki8V_K1M1FpQtLwTvb2jg/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#006400\">Werewolf</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1bpr1EjQ4RfZ5dz-tXmJJ93P2f_l7fUIUwpPLWs9Z-SI/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800080\">Mage</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1vKpSTktCUuUaqxXncG4txQPtvPclzXlFZEEX7tbrTSg/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Mummy</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Spynbcs_VgCDHdooKWXobZNe6C9CMjONeRTlvXIq9fI/edit?usp=drive_web\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Demon</span></a></b>","edited":{"userid":148,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/148-pendragon","user":"PenDragon","date":". 01-19-2016, 07:01 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/148-pendragon","name":"PenDragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar148_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1657"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-19T15:03:56-08:00","id":812155,"title":"","content":"My distaste for the tier system stems from the reason it snuck into CofD in the first place. I will not expand on that, but it didn't do the fourth wall any favors in my games. I never understood why Vampires or Werewolves cannot get Cosmic level powers, and why it is considered taboo (in a toolbox system) to get a book dealing with global and cosmic chronicles.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.greece-bynight.com\" target=\"_blank\">Greece By Night LARP</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/59-stylanski","name":"stylanski","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar59_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"299"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-19T16:19:24-08:00","id":812201,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ShadowKnight1224</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/810975-power-tiers-in-2e?p=812143#post812143\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Their usefulness doesn't lie in a white room reductionist &quot;my fave is better than your fave&quot; approach, but as a general Storyteller guide when doing crossovers.</div> </div> </div> </div> I've run true crossover games before. So, I fail to see how this kind of tier system is wrothwhile for a general Storyteller guide for crossovers. You'll excuse me if I disbelieve. Once game I ran involved coming out, an out of the coffin, all supernatural Revealed thing. But I had a good party that was spread between vamp, wolf, ling, and sin-eater. All with social skills, and all who stayed relevant and had fun. How would a ranking system help here? It wouldn't.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-19T16:34:14-08:00","id":812206,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PenDragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/810975-power-tiers-in-2e?p=812133#post812133\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The D&amp;D tier list, which I'm very familiar with, is built on the assumption that all the characters will form a party, and run through combat heavy, D&amp;D style encounters. And there's nothing wrong with that, that's how D&amp;D is expected to be played. Mind you, I've played games with Wizards who were considerably worse than the party Fighter, and Rogues who were on par with the average sorcerer. But if what you're looking for is a Tier list that ranks the splats based on the assumption that they are all collectively working as a party to defeat Storyteller placed obstacles, I can probably gander a decent one.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, even outside of combat wizards are king. Heck, I'm playing a wizard that's a demon-summoning specialist, but the fact she can cast divination, teleportation, language understanding, and the like makes her very useful. More so that merely the threat of a wizard being angry is a pretty good deterrent. That's not even getting into her knowledge checks when being an Int-focused caster with no skill dependencies. Oh and her bluff is amazing too, comes with the demon-summoning thing.<br /> <br /> I have another character (Who's not been played yet) which is basically &quot;Rogue, but with magic&quot;. She can sneak attack, cast information gathering, illusion, and mind-altering spells, as well as being a really good skill monkey.<br /> <br /> <br /> What it comes down to is versatility. In D&amp;D the fighter only has a sword, they don't have the resources to be good at everything. A caster on the other hand, they simply prepare different spells. When you compare a class that can cast in either a free-form manner or via a large menu rather than a scant few pre-determined options of course they're going to be better. It's all about synergy and flexibility. In World of Darkness Mages have their Improvisions, which basically make their options virtually unlimited. Even if they're mechanically weaker, they're not overly specialized.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9830-reshyshira","name":"ReshyShira","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9830_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"589"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-19T16:43:44-08:00","id":812209,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/810975-power-tiers-in-2e?p=812201#post812201\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I've run true crossover games before. So, I fail to see how this kind of tier system is wrothwhile for a general Storyteller guide for crossovers. You'll excuse me if I disbelieve. Once game I ran involved coming out, an out of the coffin, all supernatural Revealed thing. But I had a good party that was spread between vamp, wolf, ling, and sin-eater. All with social skills, and all who stayed relevant and had fun. How would a ranking system help here? It wouldn't.</div> </div> </div> </div>I need no help to improvise on my feet when players make sudden turns or don't act the way I expect them to, but other STs do have that problem. We are not all the same, and some things that are useless to you will be invaluable for someone else. I wouldn't knock on something that can help others.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/872434-shadow-knight-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10056-shadowknight1224","name":"ShadowKnight1224","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"975"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-19T16:51:52-08:00","id":812216,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ShadowKnight1224</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/810975-power-tiers-in-2e?p=812209#post812209\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I need no help to improvise on my feet when players make sudden turns or don't act the way I expect them to, but other STs do have that problem. We are not all the same, and some things that are useless to you will be invaluable for someone else. I wouldn't knock on something that can help others.</div> </div> </div> </div> And just -how- is it invaluable for anyone? That's the part I'm not sold on. &quot;Mages are good for games involving random problem solving quests!&quot; Unless you build a militant, combat heavy Arrow that's specialzing in magic that's not very good for being a problem solver beyond Smash! Or a magical politician/judge. Inappropriate concepts won't be carried by the virtue of being a mage. Combat heavy games won't be carried by virtue of being a werewolf with no combat focus.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2102,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","user":"MCN","date":". 01-19-2016, 07:56 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-19T17:03:20-08:00","id":812227,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/810975-power-tiers-in-2e?p=812216#post812216\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> And just -how- is it invaluable for anyone? That's the part I'm not sold on. &quot;Mages are good for games involving random problem solving quests!&quot; Unless you build a militant, combat heavy Arrow that's specialzing in magic that's not very good for being a problem solver beyond Smash! Or a magical politician/judge. Inappropriate concepts won't be carried by the virtue of being a mage. Combat heavy games won't be carried by virtue of being a werewolf with no combat focus.</div> </div> </div> </div>I already responded to everything, provided rationale and examples, in the post I made that you already quoted. For Storytellers who haven't yet instinctively grasped the capabilities, strengths and weaknesses of each line when put all together, a tier system would help them pinpoint what characters might need special attention or additional challenge.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/872434-shadow-knight-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10056-shadowknight1224","name":"ShadowKnight1224","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"975"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-19T17:05:25-08:00","id":812229,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/810975-power-tiers-in-2e?p=812216#post812216\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> And just -how- is it invaluable for anyone? That's the part I'm not sold on. &quot;Mages are good for games involving random problem solving quests!&quot; Unless you build a militant, combat heavy Arrow that's specialzing in magic that's not very good for being a problem solver beyond Smash! Or a magical politician/judge. Inappropriate concepts won't be carried by the virtue of being a mage.</div> </div> </div> </div>This. This is where the tiers really fall apart.<br /> <br /> Splats aren't classes with focused roles. If Vampires truly were &quot;the social splat&quot;, Nosferatu would be pretty well fucked. And calling all Demons master infiltrators discredits the entirely valid &quot;cover shredding war machine&quot;. Perfect in game example: I ran a game about two years back, mixed party: Purified Immortal, Changing Breed (Bees!), Promethean and Changeling. Tiers would inform you that the Changeling's social acumen would put him at the forefront as the cunning, pledge-crafting illusionist, the Prommie and Shapeshifter were meat shields, and the Immortal struggled to hold his own. The actuality was that the Immortal was the gregarious, dominant face. Shapeshifter their intel specialist (and hacker), Prommie a quesing mystic with bokor tendancies, and the changeling, Giff Muldoon, a rock stupid ogre with nil for social skills and a habit of flinging himself fists first into gunfights.<br /> <br /> Long story short: The tiers were wrong, and if I'd planned around them the game would have been a disaster.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <b>Mod Voice is <u><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">RED</span></u>*</b><br /> <i>*All other colors should be read aloud in the voice of Don Knotts</i><b>.</b> <hr /><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/18519-pendragon-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">Hacks and House Rules Hub Thread</a></b><br /> <br /> <b>CofD Hacks By Splat: <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/13vBLaS5Ua1Ez-cVyK6uFa4ssvYeIIZpoA5GQTXytfcA/edit\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Vampire</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1sqltG7X-C_MdEe00PtVOZmki8V_K1M1FpQtLwTvb2jg/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#006400\">Werewolf</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1bpr1EjQ4RfZ5dz-tXmJJ93P2f_l7fUIUwpPLWs9Z-SI/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800080\">Mage</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1vKpSTktCUuUaqxXncG4txQPtvPclzXlFZEEX7tbrTSg/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Mummy</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Spynbcs_VgCDHdooKWXobZNe6C9CMjONeRTlvXIq9fI/edit?usp=drive_web\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Demon</span></a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/148-pendragon","name":"PenDragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar148_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1657"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-19T17:09:50-08:00","id":812230,"title":"","content":"That happens, though. It's impossible to create a system that can withstand and treat all inputs with equal efficacy. I honestly can't see the downside with giving people information that, at best, would greatly help them, and at worst, would mildly inconvenience them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/872434-shadow-knight-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10056-shadowknight1224","name":"ShadowKnight1224","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"975"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-19T17:22:50-08:00","id":812236,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ShadowKnight1224</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/810975-power-tiers-in-2e?p=812230#post812230\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That happens, though. It's impossible to create a system that can withstand and treat all inputs with equal efficacy. I honestly can't see the downside with giving people information that, at best, would greatly help them, and at worst, would mildly inconvenience them.</div> </div> </div> </div>One could contest that it does harm as well as good. A person reading a tier list could take away bad advice just as much as they can good, something like: &quot;vampires and mages cannot play side by side.&quot; While what they really needed to know was: &quot;make certain each player has the opportunity to excel in their chosen area, and maybe don't pair two investigation specialists in the same game&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <b>Mod Voice is <u><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">RED</span></u>*</b><br /> <i>*All other colors should be read aloud in the voice of Don Knotts</i><b>.</b> <hr /><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/18519-pendragon-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">Hacks and House Rules Hub Thread</a></b><br /> <br /> <b>CofD Hacks By Splat: <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/13vBLaS5Ua1Ez-cVyK6uFa4ssvYeIIZpoA5GQTXytfcA/edit\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Vampire</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1sqltG7X-C_MdEe00PtVOZmki8V_K1M1FpQtLwTvb2jg/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#006400\">Werewolf</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1bpr1EjQ4RfZ5dz-tXmJJ93P2f_l7fUIUwpPLWs9Z-SI/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800080\">Mage</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1vKpSTktCUuUaqxXncG4txQPtvPclzXlFZEEX7tbrTSg/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Mummy</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Spynbcs_VgCDHdooKWXobZNe6C9CMjONeRTlvXIq9fI/edit?usp=drive_web\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Demon</span></a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/148-pendragon","name":"PenDragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar148_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1657"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-19T17:36:48-08:00","id":812246,"title":"","content":"That seems like a wording problem, not an informational/content problem.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/872434-shadow-knight-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10056-shadowknight1224","name":"ShadowKnight1224","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"975"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-19T19:54:41-08:00","id":812327,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PenDragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/810975-power-tiers-in-2e?p=812229#post812229\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This. This is where the tiers really fall apart.<br /> <br /> Splats aren't classes with focused roles. If Vampires truly were &quot;the social splat&quot;, Nosferatu would be pretty well fucked. And calling all Demons master infiltrators discredits the entirely valid &quot;cover shredding war machine&quot;. Perfect in game example: I ran a game about two years back, mixed party: Purified Immortal, Changing Breed (Bees!), Promethean and Changeling. Tiers would inform you that the Changeling's social acumen would put him at the forefront as the cunning, pledge-crafting illusionist, the Prommie and Shapeshifter were meat shields, and the Immortal struggled to hold his own. The actuality was that the Immortal was the gregarious, dominant face. Shapeshifter their intel specialist (and hacker), Prommie a quesing mystic with bokor tendancies, and the changeling, Giff Muldoon, a rock stupid ogre with nil for social skills and a habit of flinging himself fists first into gunfights.<br /> <br /> Long story short: The tiers were wrong, and if I'd planned around them the game would have been a disaster.</div> </div> </div> </div>Nope, because all of the splats are intended to be a closed-system. They're supposed to be able to stand on their own.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9830-reshyshira","name":"ReshyShira","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9830_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"589"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-19T20:22:50-08:00","id":812343,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>stylanski</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/810975-power-tiers-in-2e?p=812155#post812155\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My distaste for the tier system stems from the reason it snuck into CofD in the first place. I will not expand on that, but it didn't do the fourth wall any favors in my games. I never understood why Vampires or Werewolves cannot get Cosmic level powers, and why it is considered taboo (in a toolbox system) to get a book dealing with global and cosmic chronicles.</div> </div> </div> </div> I'm not sure really what the first part meant. Tiers was a Hunter concept originally and all it is really is just a matter of what scope the player group is dealing with in the storyline. It's not a measure of the individual potency of a splat or if it can transcend it's nature and become something more. You can have a cosmic &quot;tier&quot; Hunter story, mortals story, Werewolf story,etc. As for the latter part I think the important thing is asking &quot;Why can't Vampires or Werewolves cannot get Cosmic level powers?&quot; is honestly asking the wrong question from a development point of view. Each development team has a vision for the game world and those visions lend themselves to a default level of play, a so called vanilla chronicle. Mage doesn't dial itself all the way up to the cosmic level of interaction as a forward thrust part of the game because the Mage developer wants mages to be &quot;better&quot; than other splats any more than the street level average chronicle of Vampire or Werewolf. It's just a how some of the visions of the game have played out. In addition with stuff like the upcoming elders book for Vampire, the crazy stuff going on with that Uratha king who might not even be a Uratha at this point anymore(I don't remember it's name sorry) a lot of the games are starting to have material in that scope to play with.<br /> <br /> Word count has more to do with why we haven't seen certain things I suspect, than anything else.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-19T20:24:33-08:00","id":812344,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PenDragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/810975-power-tiers-in-2e?p=812236#post812236\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One could contest that it does harm as well as good. A person reading a tier list could take away bad advice just as much as they can good, something like: &quot;vampires and mages cannot play side by side.&quot; While what they really needed to know was: &quot;make certain each player has the opportunity to excel in their chosen area, and maybe don't pair two investigation specialists in the same game&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>I couldn't hit the like button faster on this. It's a really really good point about the purpose of splat tier lists as a tool for players and Storytellers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-20T02:33:04-08:00","id":812467,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TyrannicalRabbit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/810975-power-tiers-in-2e?p=812343#post812343\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm not sure really what the first part meant. Tiers was a Hunter concept originally and all it is really is just a matter of what scope the player group is dealing with in the storyline. It's not a measure of the individual potency of a splat or if it can transcend it's nature and become something more. You can have a cosmic &amp;quot;tier&amp;quot; Hunter story, mortals story, Werewolf story,etc. As for the latter part I think the important thing is asking &amp;quot;Why can't Vampires or Werewolves cannot get Cosmic level powers?&amp;quot; is honestly asking the wrong question from a development point of view. Each development team has a vision for the game world and those visions lend themselves to a default level of play, a so called vanilla chronicle. Mage doesn't dial itself all the way up to the cosmic level of interaction as a forward thrust part of the game because the Mage developer wants mages to be &amp;quot;better&amp;quot; than other splats any more than the street level average chronicle of Vampire or Werewolf. It's just a how some of the visions of the game have played out. In addition with stuff like the upcoming elders book for Vampire, the crazy stuff going on with that Uratha king who might not even be a Uratha at this point anymore(I don't remember it's name sorry) a lot of the games are starting to have material in that scope to play with.<br /> <br /> Word count has more to do with why we haven't seen certain things I suspect, than anything else.</div> </div> </div> </div>Don't get me wrong, I'm glad we got tiers. It just reminds me of an earlier time thatechanics implemented an anti-VtM like atmosphere of xenophobic, isolated city states with no travel or communication. When Hunter first got the system VtR resisted for a long time, the community citing game themes and such.<br /> <br /> I like Archmages, I'm glad they exist. I just don't see why Vampire shies away so much from Vampires transcend history, and Vampires as archetypal parasites of the world.<br /> <br /> I have more books of optional rules that go fully against core themes for the sake of stories (yay for thematic variety) but whenever something reminds me of how Requiem tried (and may still be trying) not to become VtM for all the wrong reasons, it disappoints me a bit.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.greece-bynight.com\" target=\"_blank\">Greece By Night LARP</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/59-stylanski","name":"stylanski","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar59_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"299"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-20T04:07:40-08:00","id":812486,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ShadowKnight1224</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/810975-power-tiers-in-2e?p=812246#post812246\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That seems like a wording problem, not an informational/content problem.</div> </div> </div> </div> You are talking to two people who have experience dealing with crossover games who are telling you that using these lists to plan have the potential for more harm than any good to a new ST. I provided a list of different supernaturals with relevant information that I actually use as guidelines, and have suggested to people running the game in the past. Do you have any actual experience in this matter, or are you just guessing? <br /> <br /> Do you know who actually needs special attention from STs in full crossover games? Mages - their magic rules are complicated as hell, and you need to understand how they work, and how drawbacks like Spell Tolerance, Spell Limit, Paradox, Unraveling, Disbelief, and Improbable work, as well as when spells need to be ritual cast instead of allowing Instant magic. Its necessary for a big part of the splat's themes, or they stop feeling like mages. Do you know who else? Sin-Eaters and wolves. They get Essence / Plasm from dealing with spirits and ghosts, or tied to a locus/haunt. So, you're either tied to a specific location, or need dedicated &quot;feeding scenes.&quot; Or have a player that designs a PC based on essence / plasm efficency - I ran a SE once that never actually needed to deal with ghosts or haunts, and could recharge plasm through Virtue/Vice; it wasn't easy, but doable. Do you know who doesn't need special attention? Ordo Dracul vampires. But would you know any of this from any tier ratings? No. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TyrannicalRabbit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/810975-power-tiers-in-2e?p=812343#post812343\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not sure really what the first part meant. Tiers was a Hunter concept originally and all it is really is just a matter of what scope the player group is dealing with in the storyline. It's not a measure of the individual potency of a splat or if it can transcend it's nature and become something more. You can have a cosmic &quot;tier&quot; Hunter story, mortals story, Werewolf story,etc. As for the latter part I think the important thing is asking &quot;Why can't Vampires or Werewolves cannot get Cosmic level powers?&quot; is honestly asking the wrong question from a development point of view. Each development team has a vision for the game world and those visions lend themselves to a default level of play, a so called vanilla chronicle. Mage doesn't dial itself all the way up to the cosmic level of interaction as a forward thrust part of the game because the Mage developer wants mages to be &quot;better&quot; than other splats any more than the street level average chronicle of Vampire or Werewolf. It's just a how some of the visions of the game have played out. In addition with stuff like the upcoming elders book for Vampire, the crazy stuff going on with that Uratha king who might not even be a Uratha at this point anymore(I don't remember it's name sorry) a lot of the games are starting to have material in that scope to play with.<br /> <br /> Word count has more to do with why we haven't seen certain things I suspect, than anything else.</div> </div> </div> </div> Actually, I'm fairly sure that the tier system was thrown out because it actually did more harm than good, iirc. I think there was a blog post that mentioned it. People started thinking in terms of straight jackets and defined blocks that couldn't be budged, when the tiers were supposed to be meant as an aid. If tier 2 is city-wide, and tier 3 is global, what do you call a game that spans three or so US states and a bit of Canada? What about when when tier 1 hunters join together to form a power bloc to protect their city? Is a Lucifuge not allowed to set up shop and worry just about his few bloody blocks he protects? Games needed to be more flexible than the tier system allowed. <br /> <br /> Honestly, the tier system existed when the first three games came out. It seems like, to me, that Werewolf, with its focus on pack over any larger organization, is a tier 1 game, city-focused Vampire was tier 2, and Mage with its global scale concerns is a tier 3 game. And yet, each of those games shift and change a lot. Mage, despite having global connections, is often hyper focused on individual Obsessions or what the local Seers are doing than some grand world wide chess game. Vampires are fairly mobile, and its not unheard of for covenants between cities to organize and talk and plan together - Carthians are renowned for it in some places, especially for their trouble makers who start a rebellion, then move on. Werewolves form protectorates.<br /> <br /> So, it really came down to the question of asking how beneficial the tier system was, and how much it helped stories versus hindering them. Combined with the fact that I'm fairly sure that the system itself kept being redefined. Fairly sure that Mage used a different system than everyone else, which led to confusion. Why keep something that only causes confusion?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-20T09:17:54-08:00","id":812663,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/810975-power-tiers-in-2e?p=812486#post812486\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> You are talking to two people who have experience dealing with crossover games who are telling you that using these lists to plan have the potential for more harm than any good to a new ST. I provided a list of different supernaturals with relevant information that I actually use as guidelines, and have suggested to people running the game in the past. Do you have any actual experience in this matter, or are you just guessing?</div> </div> </div> </div>All the games I've run have technically been crossovers, and I've been an on-and-off White Wolf fan since the oWoD days. So yes, I do have quite a few years of experience on the matter.<br /> <br /> My take on this is that more options and information can't hurt, as forewarned is forearmed. But clearly this is a very sensitive matter to you, so I won't push it any further.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/872434-shadow-knight-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10056-shadowknight1224","name":"ShadowKnight1224","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"975"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-20T09:46:55-08:00","id":812686,"title":"","content":"Reading this thread, perhaps a traditional &quot;catch-all&quot; Tier system is not enough because of the sheer... breadth and flexability in each splat.<br /> <br /> We might as well have like 5 separate scoring mechanics and rate splats based on a variety of tools, because ultimately, CofD is way too flexible of a game.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/607039-homebrew-mechs-walkers-ect\" target=\"_blank\">Mechs:</a> Because even the Chronicles of Darkness needs robot fights.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/813387-darkframe-a-far-future-crossover-setting\" target=\"_blank\">DarkFrame</a>: Crossover setting that puts Chronicles of Darkness in the far future that is Warframe.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless\" target=\"_blank\">Monarch: The Endless</a> You are an alien ruler, charged with maintaining a people who you shape to suit your needs.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7015-almarck","name":"Almarck","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-20T09:54:14-08:00","id":812691,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ShadowKnight1224</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/810975-power-tiers-in-2e?p=812663#post812663\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> All the games I've run have technically been crossovers, and I've been an on-and-off White Wolf fan since the oWoD days. So yes, I do have quite a few years of experience on the matter.<br /> <br /> My take on this is that more options and information can't hurt, as forewarned is forearmed. But clearly this is a very sensitive matter to you, so I won't push it any further.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> This isn't about sensitive, or more information. This is actually fighting AGAINST disinformation. Such tier lists will disinform people more than they will inform them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B5_EJSgV1u4SOFFJc3M5VmFDWVk?resourcekey=0-GEErNnDbGqlKYgoiuGausw&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Bloodline conversions</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1IbeKfqhWuG8jPN9vpGmDo0VY9n9-4ejxvRzfJRoir4k/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My House rules</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/294-griautis","name":"Griautis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar294_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-20T10:04:32-08:00","id":812693,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Griautis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/810975-power-tiers-in-2e?p=812691#post812691\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This isn't about sensitive, or more information. This is actually fighting AGAINST disinformation. Such tier lists will disinform people more than they will inform them.</div> </div> </div> </div>Disinformation is done deliberately, which is not the case here.<br /> <br /> If you mean misinformation, I think that's a poor argument to make, when such a risk is common in many informational endeavours, and many steps can be taken to avoid or minimise it.<br /> <br /> I think the problem is not misinformation. I think tier lists have been so controversial that a lot of people have a kneejerk reaction towards them, perhaps due to the idea that it will somehow adversely affect the different gamelines.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/872434-shadow-knight-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10056-shadowknight1224","name":"ShadowKnight1224","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"975"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-20T10:08:34-08:00","id":812697,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Almarck</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/810975-power-tiers-in-2e?p=812686#post812686\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Reading this thread, perhaps a traditional &quot;catch-all&quot; Tier system is not enough because of the sheer... breadth and flexability in each splat.<br /> <br /> We might as well have like 5 separate scoring mechanics and rate splats based on a variety of tools, because ultimately, CofD is way too flexible of a game.</div> </div> </div> </div>Why do we need that?<br /> <br /> It's not like tier lists are terribly accurate. We can say &quot;vampires are tier 3 stealth characters&quot;, but unless you've invested in Obfuscate (or maybe Protean) that's not gonna hold true. Even template statements like &quot;Werewolves are Tier 1 brawlers&quot;, are wholly dependent on the characters and context around them. Tier lists aren't even perfectly accurate for games that are easily tier-able, look at the <a href=\"http://www.eventhubs.com/tiers/sf4/\" target=\"_blank\">tiers for Street Fighter IV</a> reading those one might be lead to believe that everyone should be playing Yun, Evil Ryu or Cammy? I mean, they're top tier and SF players play to win. But the <a href=\"http://shoryuken.com/2015/07/19/evo-2015-day-1-results-the-largest-fighting-game-tournament-in-the-world/\" target=\"_blank\">Evo top 25</a> shows an absolutely massive character variety. If even a white room brawler's tiers are dubious how on earth can anyone expect CofD tiers to be accurate?<br /> <br /> Tier lists are only true (and debatable even then) for the abstract concept of the splat, the idealized Promethean with all Transmutations and Bestowments. But they invoke in people assumptions about how a splat is supposed to perform that is, IMO, far more detrimental to crossover than any power disparity.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <b>Mod Voice is <u><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">RED</span></u>*</b><br /> <i>*All other colors should be read aloud in the voice of Don Knotts</i><b>.</b> <hr /><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/18519-pendragon-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">Hacks and House Rules Hub Thread</a></b><br /> <br /> <b>CofD Hacks By Splat: <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/13vBLaS5Ua1Ez-cVyK6uFa4ssvYeIIZpoA5GQTXytfcA/edit\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Vampire</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1sqltG7X-C_MdEe00PtVOZmki8V_K1M1FpQtLwTvb2jg/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#006400\">Werewolf</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1bpr1EjQ4RfZ5dz-tXmJJ93P2f_l7fUIUwpPLWs9Z-SI/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800080\">Mage</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1vKpSTktCUuUaqxXncG4txQPtvPclzXlFZEEX7tbrTSg/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Mummy</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Spynbcs_VgCDHdooKWXobZNe6C9CMjONeRTlvXIq9fI/edit?usp=drive_web\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Demon</span></a></b>","edited":{"userid":148,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/148-pendragon","user":"PenDragon","date":". 01-20-2016, 01:13 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/148-pendragon","name":"PenDragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar148_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1657"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-20T11:41:35-08:00","id":812761,"title":"","content":"Tier lists measure a classes potential, not necessarily what each and every character belonging to that class is going to achieve. Wizards are Tier 1, but that doesn't mean they can't be built terribly or played in a way that they are less useful than a Tier 3 or Tier 4 character. Wizards excel at being high intelligence casters and are Tier 1 based on the assumption that they're building towards what they're best at. That doesn't mean there isn't some 20 strength 12 intelligence wizards running around out there tossing around cantrips while punching people in the face. The same applies here. If a tier list says that something is a Tier X Y, then it's listing that whatever it is has the <i>potential</i> to be a Tier X Y, not that it will always be that regardless of build.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2309-ashenrogue","name":"Ashenrogue","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1388"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-20T12:18:11-08:00","id":812775,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PenDragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/810975-power-tiers-in-2e?p=812697#post812697\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But they invoke in people assumptions about how a splat is supposed to perform that is, IMO, far more detrimental to crossover than any power disparity.</div> </div> </div> </div>Agreed. Worse yet, these assumptions have sunk into the community hive mind, limiting the types of stories expected to be playable in certain splats (thus feeding into what books get written or not).<br /> <br /> I want my Requiem chronicle through the ages, dammit! Legalize Methuselahs already! :'( <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.greece-bynight.com\" target=\"_blank\">Greece By Night LARP</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/59-stylanski","name":"stylanski","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar59_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"299"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-20T12:31:33-08:00","id":812786,"title":"","content":"Alright, assuming we try to construct a tier list, what's the metric? D&amp;D's tier list works partially because of the game's base assumptions; that everyone is going to form a party and go adventuring together, encountering roughly four or so challenges each day. So how do we define CofD? Is it a game of &quot;Visceral drama and personal horror&quot;? &quot;Phantom threats and savage fury&quot;? or is it about &quot;awe inspiring truths and deadly hubris&quot;? Or is it some other splat's pitch phrase? The answer: it depends on the splat and storyteller.<br /> <br /> So how do we tier, in a way that is even mildly useful, the splats?<ul><li><b>We could go the D&amp;D route: raw problem solving ability</b>. But while that works for D&amp;D, where everyone is expected to be a buddy-buddy genocide squad <u>opposing</u> the DM's vicious schemes, it doesn't exactly reflect how CofD is played. Notably it makes no account for story, character and motivation which are <b>essential</b> to the Storytelling system.</li> <li><b>We could go with the oft proposed five point statistic grid</b>. Breaking each splat down by how their skill in each category. But that'll be comparing apples and oranges. Each splat has their own exceedingly different way of approaching every scenario, and it's hard to call one universally better than the other when the tiers can flip the instant the scenario changes.</li> <li><b>We could break down each splat by how they play into other splats games</b>. Which, IMO, is the only truly viable option. But that creates ten different tier lists, more as splats are added, and at that point why bother tiering them at all? Why not just write a really indepth guide to crossover addressing each splat?</li> </ul>In the end we return to the question, what good is this doing? Because I've seen what the old tier lists do, and that's generate pages of bitching about Mage supremacy, imbalanced starting dots, and the (supposedly) tragic absence of Arch[Insert Splat Here]s.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <b>Mod Voice is <u><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">RED</span></u>*</b><br /> <i>*All other colors should be read aloud in the voice of Don Knotts</i><b>.</b> <hr /><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/18519-pendragon-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">Hacks and House Rules Hub Thread</a></b><br /> <br /> <b>CofD Hacks By Splat: <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/13vBLaS5Ua1Ez-cVyK6uFa4ssvYeIIZpoA5GQTXytfcA/edit\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Vampire</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1sqltG7X-C_MdEe00PtVOZmki8V_K1M1FpQtLwTvb2jg/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#006400\">Werewolf</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1bpr1EjQ4RfZ5dz-tXmJJ93P2f_l7fUIUwpPLWs9Z-SI/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800080\">Mage</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1vKpSTktCUuUaqxXncG4txQPtvPclzXlFZEEX7tbrTSg/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Mummy</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Spynbcs_VgCDHdooKWXobZNe6C9CMjONeRTlvXIq9fI/edit?usp=drive_web\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Demon</span></a></b>","edited":{"userid":148,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/148-pendragon","user":"PenDragon","date":". 01-20-2016, 04:04 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/148-pendragon","name":"PenDragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar148_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1657"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-20T12:47:19-08:00","id":812803,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PenDragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/810975-power-tiers-in-2e?p=812786#post812786\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Alright, assuming we try to construct a tier list, what's the metric? D&amp;D's tier list works partially because of the game's base assumptions; that everyone is going to form a party and go adventuring together, encountering roughly four or so challenges each day. So how do we define CofD? Is it a game of &quot;Visceral drama and personal horror&quot;? &quot;Phantom threats and savage fury&quot;? or is it about &quot;awe inspiring truths and deadly hubris&quot;? Or is it some other splat's pitch phrase? The answer: it depends on the splat and storyteller.<br /> <br /> So how to we tier, in a way that is even mildly useful, the splats?<ul><li><b>We could go the D&amp;D route: raw problem solving ability</b>. But while that works for D&amp;D, where everyone is expected to be a buddy-buddy genocide squad <u>opposing</u> the DM's vicious schemes, it doesn't exactly reflect how CofD is played. Notably it makes no account for story, character and motivation which are <b>essential</b> to the Storytelling system.</li> <li><b>We could go with the oft proposed five point statistic grid</b>. Breaking each splat down by how their skill in each category. But that'll be comparing apples and oranges. Each splat has their own exceedingly different way of approaching every scenario, and it's hard to call one universally better than the other when the tiers can flip the instant the scenario changes.</li> <li><b>We could break down each splat by how they play into other splats games</b>. Which, IMO, is the only truly viable option. But that creates ten different tier lists, more as splats are added, and at that point why bother tiering them at all? Why not just write a really indepth guide to crossover addressing each splat?</li> </ul><br /> In the end we return to the question, what good is this doing? Because I've seen what the old tier lists do, and that's generate pages of bitching about Mage supremacy, imbalanced starting dots, and the (supposedly) tragic absence of Arch[Insert Splat Here]s.</div> </div> </div> </div>I dunno, Tiers really only apply in games where there is expected overlap. I mean you can obviously construct one, but the games weren't designed with overlap in mind. So I can't really say for sure if it's necessary. However, the thing is how do you provide a metric or framework for how well different splats work together? I believe that's more about what people are concerned about. It should be less about raw power and more about compatibility.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9830-reshyshira","name":"ReshyShira","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9830_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"589"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-20T13:04:13-08:00","id":812825,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ReshyShira</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/810975-power-tiers-in-2e?p=812803#post812803\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I dunno, Tiers really only apply in games where there is expected overlap. I mean you can obviously construct one, but the games weren't designed with overlap in mind. So I can't really say for sure if it's necessary. However, the thing is how do you provide a metric or framework for how well different splats work together? I believe that's more about what people are concerned about. It should be less about raw power and more about compatibility.</div> </div> </div> </div>That would be the point I'm trying to get across.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <b>Mod Voice is <u><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">RED</span></u>*</b><br /> <i>*All other colors should be read aloud in the voice of Don Knotts</i><b>.</b> <hr /><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/18519-pendragon-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">Hacks and House Rules Hub Thread</a></b><br /> <br /> <b>CofD Hacks By Splat: <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/13vBLaS5Ua1Ez-cVyK6uFa4ssvYeIIZpoA5GQTXytfcA/edit\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Vampire</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1sqltG7X-C_MdEe00PtVOZmki8V_K1M1FpQtLwTvb2jg/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#006400\">Werewolf</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1bpr1EjQ4RfZ5dz-tXmJJ93P2f_l7fUIUwpPLWs9Z-SI/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800080\">Mage</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1vKpSTktCUuUaqxXncG4txQPtvPclzXlFZEEX7tbrTSg/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Mummy</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Spynbcs_VgCDHdooKWXobZNe6C9CMjONeRTlvXIq9fI/edit?usp=drive_web\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Demon</span></a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/148-pendragon","name":"PenDragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar148_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1657"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-20T13:07:36-08:00","id":812829,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PenDragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/810975-power-tiers-in-2e?p=812825#post812825\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That would be the point I'm trying to get across.</div> </div> </div> </div>Then we agree, right? So, can anything be done about it?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9830-reshyshira","name":"ReshyShira","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9830_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"589"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-20T13:16:05-08:00","id":812840,"title":"","content":"I'm going to assume good faith here, so I'll propose a potential tier system for crossovers that doesn't misinform or overlook player choice.<br /> <br /> The answer is actually simple: You don't list the splats in tiers, you list their <i>mechanics</i>.<br /> <br /> So instead of <b>Stealth: Tier 2: Vampire</b>, you state <b>Stealth: Tier 2: Obfuscate (Vampire Discipline)</b>. It will then become implicit that if the vampire character in your chronicle does not possess that Discipline, they will not be Tier 2 in Stealth.<br /> <br /> The tiers would then be divided according to mechanical capabilities. Off the top of my head, I could see a tier in every major subsystem (Investigation, Chases, etc.) and then a subdivision of the main core systems (combat, social manouvering, etc.) and then we can include some common plot elements, to see what mechanics are the most suited to deal with them (for example, character imprisonment, a murder mystery, mortals discovering the character's true nature, etc.).<br /> <br /> Would it be a very long and diverse tier list? Absolutely. Would it be very useful for crossovers and general Storyteller learning? Damn right.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/872434-shadow-knight-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10056-shadowknight1224","name":"ShadowKnight1224","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"975"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-20T13:29:48-08:00","id":812856,"title":"","content":"Let me pose this question: Why tiers? What do tiers offer that a comprehensive breakdown of splat aptitudes and themes does not?<br /> <br /> Because the only advantage I'm seeing is that it's concise. Like a cooking cheat sheet, someone can look at a tier list an develop an immediate idea of what goes well with what. Of course the tier list doesn't tell you that Vampires can't do shit with the Shadow, and a Werewolf / Vampire crossover that fails to address this issue will be plagued with dissonance. But they create a very compelling <b>illusion</b> of order. And people love order.<br /> <br /> Sure you could expand it, address the X and Y of each splat, compare and contrast Disciplines with Embeds, but the more words you add the hard it is to grasp at a glance, and the harder becomes to put into a tiered order. In the end a detailed enough tier list is really no better than just reading the effing core books. Hence I am unconvinced of their utility.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <b>Mod Voice is <u><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">RED</span></u>*</b><br /> <i>*All other colors should be read aloud in the voice of Don Knotts</i><b>.</b> <hr /><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/18519-pendragon-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">Hacks and House Rules Hub Thread</a></b><br /> <br /> <b>CofD Hacks By Splat: <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/13vBLaS5Ua1Ez-cVyK6uFa4ssvYeIIZpoA5GQTXytfcA/edit\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Vampire</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1sqltG7X-C_MdEe00PtVOZmki8V_K1M1FpQtLwTvb2jg/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#006400\">Werewolf</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1bpr1EjQ4RfZ5dz-tXmJJ93P2f_l7fUIUwpPLWs9Z-SI/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800080\">Mage</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1vKpSTktCUuUaqxXncG4txQPtvPclzXlFZEEX7tbrTSg/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Mummy</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Spynbcs_VgCDHdooKWXobZNe6C9CMjONeRTlvXIq9fI/edit?usp=drive_web\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Demon</span></a></b>","edited":{"userid":148,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/148-pendragon","user":"PenDragon","date":". 01-20-2016, 04:33 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/148-pendragon","name":"PenDragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar148_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1657"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-20T13:36:18-08:00","id":812862,"title":"","content":"You underestimate the value of information consolidation, which allows for comparing and contrasting efficiently, without flavour text getting in the way, or having to tab between different PDF files or have ten books taking up the entirety surface of a table. Not to mention that, as you do your comparisons, you might be inclined to take notes in order to better remember/access the information during play. And at that point, isn't a properly organised system a lot more efficient?<br /> <br /> As for why tiers in particular, no reason other than it's something people are familiar with and can grasp intuitively.<br /> <br /> Personally, I'm not married to the tier system itself, but I will unwaveringly support any form of information consolidation that can help Storytellers and players.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/872434-shadow-knight-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10056-shadowknight1224","name":"ShadowKnight1224","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"975"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-20T13:57:53-08:00","id":812878,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>stylanski</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/810975-power-tiers-in-2e?p=812467#post812467\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Don't get me wrong, I'm glad we got tiers. It just reminds me of an earlier time thatechanics implemented an anti-VtM like atmosphere of xenophobic, isolated city states with no travel or communication. When Hunter first got the system VtR resisted for a long time, the community citing game themes and such.<br /> <br /> I like Archmages, I'm glad they exist. I just don't see why Vampire shies away so much from Vampires transcend history, and Vampires as archetypal parasites of the world.<br /> <br /> I have more books of optional rules that go fully against core themes for the sake of stories (yay for thematic variety) but whenever something reminds me of how Requiem tried (and may still be trying) not to become VtM for all the wrong reasons, it disappoints me a bit.</div> </div> </div> </div>Why tiers were made at first and why the idea was dropped is not the same thing as a developer's vision for the default setting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2997,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/","user":"Guest","date":". 01-20-2016, 05:13 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-20T14:11:53-08:00","id":812886,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ShadowKnight1224</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/810975-power-tiers-in-2e?p=812862#post812862\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You underestimate the value of information consolidation, which allows for comparing and contrasting efficiently, without flavour text getting in the way, or having to tab between different PDF files or have ten books taking up the entirety surface of a table. Not to mention that, as you do your comparisons, you might be inclined to take notes in order to better remember/access the information during play. And at that point, isn't a properly organised system a lot more efficient?<br /> <br /> As for why tiers in particular, no reason other than it's something people are familiar with and can grasp intuitively.<br /> <br /> Personally, I'm not married to the tier system itself, but I will unwaveringly support any form of information consolidation that can help Storytellers and players.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh I'd never doubt the value of consolidation, the wod canon index is a godsend for that reason, and I truly wish the books had more accessible cheat sheets somewhere at the back.<br /> <br /> No, what I doubt is the veracity of the information. Is Obfuscate worse than the Mind Arcana? Because that's what a tier list is going to imply, better and worse. And I don't think that's terribly helpful to anyone.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <b>Mod Voice is <u><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">RED</span></u>*</b><br /> <i>*All other colors should be read aloud in the voice of Don Knotts</i><b>.</b> <hr /><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/18519-pendragon-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">Hacks and House Rules Hub Thread</a></b><br /> <br /> <b>CofD Hacks By Splat: <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/13vBLaS5Ua1Ez-cVyK6uFa4ssvYeIIZpoA5GQTXytfcA/edit\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Vampire</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1sqltG7X-C_MdEe00PtVOZmki8V_K1M1FpQtLwTvb2jg/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#006400\">Werewolf</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1bpr1EjQ4RfZ5dz-tXmJJ93P2f_l7fUIUwpPLWs9Z-SI/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800080\">Mage</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1vKpSTktCUuUaqxXncG4txQPtvPclzXlFZEEX7tbrTSg/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Mummy</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Spynbcs_VgCDHdooKWXobZNe6C9CMjONeRTlvXIq9fI/edit?usp=drive_web\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Demon</span></a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/148-pendragon","name":"PenDragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar148_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1657"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-20T14:15:33-08:00","id":812887,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PenDragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/810975-power-tiers-in-2e?p=812886#post812886\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh I'd never doubt the value of consolidation, the wod canon index is a godsend for that reason, and I truly wish the books had more accessible cheat sheets somewhere at the back.<br /> <br /> No, what I doubt is the veracity of the information. Is Obfuscate worse than the Mind Arcana? Because that's what a tier list is going to imply, better and worse. And I don't think that's terribly helpful to anyone.</div> </div> </div> </div>Maybe focus it based on how well a splat can handle certain situations? Eg. How good is a Werewolf at investigation compared to say a Demon. The metric for what &quot;good&quot; means would probably be breadth of options. Obviously all have an investigation skill, as do hunters, but beyond that what do they have? How many resources does it take to be good at it? How potent are the options?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":9830,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9830-reshyshira","user":"ReshyShira","date":". 01-20-2016, 05:38 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9830-reshyshira","name":"ReshyShira","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9830_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"589"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-20T14:30:25-08:00","id":812899,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PenDragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/810975-power-tiers-in-2e?p=812886#post812886\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is Obfuscate worse than the Mind Arcana? Because that's what a tier list is going to imply, better and worse. And I don't think that's terribly helpful to anyone.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well if you go off D&amp;D/PF style tiers, then yes Obfuscate is much much much worse than the mind arcana. Because it is much less versatile and each dot of obfuscate is very specific in it's abilities while the Mind Arcana can accomplish the same stuff as Obfuscate and more in general because of how you can use the Mind Arcana to do anything related to the mind rather than just obscure things.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-20T14:44:25-08:00","id":812917,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>milo v3</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/810975-power-tiers-in-2e?p=812899#post812899\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well if you go off D&amp;D/PF style tiers, then yes Obfuscate is much much much worse than the mind arcana. Because it is much less versatile and each dot of obfuscate is very specific in it's abilities while the Mind Arcana can accomplish the same stuff as Obfuscate and more in general because of how you can use the Mind Arcana to do anything related to the mind rather than just obscure things.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, if we go by the D&amp;D tier standards we can create a very convincing, decisively misleading tier list. One that puts Mages and Demons at the top (thanks to their enormously flexible powers) but forgets to mention that their inherent themes will put them at odds in almost any crossover not explicitly planned to circumvent them. I wouldn't call that a terribly helpful guide.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <b>Mod Voice is <u><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">RED</span></u>*</b><br /> <i>*All other colors should be read aloud in the voice of Don Knotts</i><b>.</b> <hr /><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/18519-pendragon-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">Hacks and House Rules Hub Thread</a></b><br /> <br /> <b>CofD Hacks By Splat: <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/13vBLaS5Ua1Ez-cVyK6uFa4ssvYeIIZpoA5GQTXytfcA/edit\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Vampire</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1sqltG7X-C_MdEe00PtVOZmki8V_K1M1FpQtLwTvb2jg/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#006400\">Werewolf</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1bpr1EjQ4RfZ5dz-tXmJJ93P2f_l7fUIUwpPLWs9Z-SI/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800080\">Mage</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1vKpSTktCUuUaqxXncG4txQPtvPclzXlFZEEX7tbrTSg/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Mummy</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Spynbcs_VgCDHdooKWXobZNe6C9CMjONeRTlvXIq9fI/edit?usp=drive_web\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Demon</span></a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/148-pendragon","name":"PenDragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar148_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1657"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-20T14:53:46-08:00","id":812933,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PenDragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/810975-power-tiers-in-2e?p=812917#post812917\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes, if we go by the D&amp;D tier standards we can create a very convincing, decisively misleading tier list. One that puts Mages and Demons at the top (thanks to their enormously flexible powers) but forgets to mention that their inherent themes will put them at odds in almost any crossover not explicitly planned to circumvent them. I wouldn't call that a terribly helpful guide.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm actually playing a Demon/Mage crossover right now.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9830-reshyshira","name":"ReshyShira","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9830_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"589"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-20T15:11:00-08:00","id":812944,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ReshyShira</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/810975-power-tiers-in-2e?p=812933#post812933\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm actually playing a Demon/Mage crossover right now.</div> </div> </div> </div>Demon / Mage has really great crossover potential. The Investigator vs Spy angle is cool, their powers feel very similar in style (hacking reality) and, when they can trust eachother, Mages and Demons shore up one another's faults quite nicely. However, one needs to understand and prepare for the &quot;Mages love mysteries, and Demons hate being investigated&quot; angle of the game or they'll run into complications down the line.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <b>Mod Voice is <u><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">RED</span></u>*</b><br /> <i>*All other colors should be read aloud in the voice of Don Knotts</i><b>.</b> <hr /><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/18519-pendragon-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">Hacks and House Rules Hub Thread</a></b><br /> <br /> <b>CofD Hacks By Splat: <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/13vBLaS5Ua1Ez-cVyK6uFa4ssvYeIIZpoA5GQTXytfcA/edit\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Vampire</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1sqltG7X-C_MdEe00PtVOZmki8V_K1M1FpQtLwTvb2jg/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#006400\">Werewolf</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1bpr1EjQ4RfZ5dz-tXmJJ93P2f_l7fUIUwpPLWs9Z-SI/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800080\">Mage</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1vKpSTktCUuUaqxXncG4txQPtvPclzXlFZEEX7tbrTSg/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Mummy</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Spynbcs_VgCDHdooKWXobZNe6C9CMjONeRTlvXIq9fI/edit?usp=drive_web\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Demon</span></a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/148-pendragon","name":"PenDragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar148_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1657"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-20T15:16:49-08:00","id":812948,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PenDragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/810975-power-tiers-in-2e?p=812917#post812917\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes, if we go by the D&amp;D tier standards we can create a very convincing, decisively misleading tier list. One that puts Mages and Demons at the top (thanks to their enormously flexible powers) but forgets to mention that their inherent themes will put them at odds in almost any crossover not explicitly planned to circumvent them. I wouldn't call that a terribly helpful guide.</div> </div> </div> </div>Do you realize one of the themes of both Mage and Demon are &quot;Okay we can do basically anything, but can we risk doing it?&quot; and another is &quot;Okay we can do basically anything, but is it ethical to do so?&quot; right..... Their themes want them to be high tier....","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":8331,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","user":"milo v3","date":". 01-20-2016, 06:22 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-20T15:18:12-08:00","id":812949,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PenDragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/810975-power-tiers-in-2e?p=812944#post812944\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Demon / Mage has really great crossover potential. The Investigator vs Spy angle is cool, their powers feel very similar in style (hacking reality) and, when they can trust eachother, Mages and Demons shore up one another's faults quite nicely. However, one needs to understand and prepare for the &quot;Mages love mysteries, and Demons hate being investigated&quot; angle of the game or they'll run into complications down the line.</div> </div> </div> </div>We only started a little while ago, but one demon got outed almost instantly. Probably because he thought that hiding in the shadow of a cabal of mages with mage sight going is a good idea. Good thing I'm not connected to that demon in any particular way. I'm just playing my cover, she's an analyst so she makes very carefully calculated decisions before acting. They're busy thinking she's a nosy policewomen.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9830-reshyshira","name":"ReshyShira","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9830_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"589"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-20T15:23:15-08:00","id":812953,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>milo v3</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/810975-power-tiers-in-2e?p=812948#post812948\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do you realize one of the themes of both Mage and Demon are &quot;Okay we can do basically anything, but can we risk doing it?&quot; right..... Their themes want them to be high tier....</div> </div> </div> </div>No, no. I get that, it's one of the reasons they pair well. I was merely pointing out that Tier lists fail to highlight any of the subtleties of running the two splats together. Leading the the appearance that they'll go together like jam and toast, which is not always the case.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <b>Mod Voice is <u><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">RED</span></u>*</b><br /> <i>*All other colors should be read aloud in the voice of Don Knotts</i><b>.</b> <hr /><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/18519-pendragon-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">Hacks and House Rules Hub Thread</a></b><br /> <br /> <b>CofD Hacks By Splat: <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/13vBLaS5Ua1Ez-cVyK6uFa4ssvYeIIZpoA5GQTXytfcA/edit\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Vampire</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1sqltG7X-C_MdEe00PtVOZmki8V_K1M1FpQtLwTvb2jg/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#006400\">Werewolf</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1bpr1EjQ4RfZ5dz-tXmJJ93P2f_l7fUIUwpPLWs9Z-SI/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800080\">Mage</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1vKpSTktCUuUaqxXncG4txQPtvPclzXlFZEEX7tbrTSg/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Mummy</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Spynbcs_VgCDHdooKWXobZNe6C9CMjONeRTlvXIq9fI/edit?usp=drive_web\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Demon</span></a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/148-pendragon","name":"PenDragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar148_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1657"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-20T15:27:07-08:00","id":812959,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PenDragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/810975-power-tiers-in-2e?p=812786#post812786\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">[/LIST]In the end we return to the question, what good is this doing? Because I've seen what the old tier lists do, and that's generate pages of bitching about Mage supremacy, imbalanced starting dots, and the (supposedly) tragic absence of Arch[Insert Splat Here]s.</div> </div> </div> </div>You misunderstood me. I don't want Vampires or Werewolves to rival Mages by getting Arch[Insert Splat Here]. In my games, even in crossovers, I give Mages (for example) access only to the creative thaumaturgy system from Blood Sorcery. Lupines often get Protean, Vigor, plus another couple of disciplines depending on the character's background. Similarly, I would run a game of Archmages by giving access to the other splats to the same kind of powers that Mages get.<br /> <br /> I <i>bitch</i> (sorry PenDragon, couldn't resist <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" />) because I like what Mage has done (give the finger to WoD and move on with its life by going ahead and cranking up the power dial for the sake of allowing players and STs to explore more of the universe) and hope that <i>at least</i> the rest of the Three Big Ones (Mage, Werewolf, Vampire) should also have the opportunity to offer that kind of breadth of different levels of play.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.greece-bynight.com\" target=\"_blank\">Greece By Night LARP</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/59-stylanski","name":"stylanski","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar59_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"299"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-20T15:35:59-08:00","id":812966,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>stylanski</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/810975-power-tiers-in-2e?p=812959#post812959\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You misunderstood me. I don't want Vampires or Werewolves to rival Mages by getting Arch[Insert Splat Here]. In my games, even in crossovers, I give Mages (for example) access only to the creative thaumaturgy system from Blood Sorcery. Lupines often get Protean, Vigor, plus another couple of disciplines depending on the character's background. Similarly, I would run a game of Archmages by giving access to the other splats to the same kind of powers that Mages get.<br /> <br /> I <i>bitch</i> (sorry PenDragon, couldn't resist <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" />) because I like what Mage has done (give the finger to WoD and move on with its life by going ahead and cranking up the power dial for the sake of allowing players and STs to explore more of the universe) and hope that <i>at least</i> the rest of the Three Big Ones (Mage, Werewolf, Vampire) should also have the opportunity to offer that kind of breadth of different levels of play.</div> </div> </div> </div>That comment was certainly not directed at you. I'd forgotten you'd brought it up otherwise I'd have noted that. It was, in fact, not directed at anyone. Evolved splat threads tend to spiral into bitter argument, even between normally courteous individuals.<br /> <br /> No harm, no foul.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <b>Mod Voice is <u><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">RED</span></u>*</b><br /> <i>*All other colors should be read aloud in the voice of Don Knotts</i><b>.</b> <hr /><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/18519-pendragon-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">Hacks and House Rules Hub Thread</a></b><br /> <br /> <b>CofD Hacks By Splat: <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/13vBLaS5Ua1Ez-cVyK6uFa4ssvYeIIZpoA5GQTXytfcA/edit\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Vampire</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1sqltG7X-C_MdEe00PtVOZmki8V_K1M1FpQtLwTvb2jg/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#006400\">Werewolf</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1bpr1EjQ4RfZ5dz-tXmJJ93P2f_l7fUIUwpPLWs9Z-SI/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800080\">Mage</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1vKpSTktCUuUaqxXncG4txQPtvPclzXlFZEEX7tbrTSg/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Mummy</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Spynbcs_VgCDHdooKWXobZNe6C9CMjONeRTlvXIq9fI/edit?usp=drive_web\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Demon</span></a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/148-pendragon","name":"PenDragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar148_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1657"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-20T15:48:37-08:00","id":812971,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PenDragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/810975-power-tiers-in-2e?p=812953#post812953\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No, no. I get that, it's one of the reasons they pair well. I was merely pointing out that Tier lists fail to highlight any of the subtleties of running the two splats together. Leading the the appearance that they'll go together like jam and toast, which is not always the case.</div> </div> </div> </div>Tiers don't make it look like two things go well together in my experience, merely highlights the versatility and options that each Class/Splat has. I mean, you can make a wizard and fighter team that works amazingly, regardless of the fact that both are on opposite ends of the tier list, or have a cleric who overshadows the groups witch despite the fact they are both tier 1. Tiers in CofD would serve to show how much power and versatility the different splats have. A vampire is useful in less scenarios than a mage, since a vampire will be much more specialized than a mage of the same experience would be. They both would have different strengths as individuals, have different resources, different allies, different etc, but the mage is still able to do much more than the vampire in general. Both can be completely valid characters next to each other of course, especially if they focus on different fields.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":8331,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","user":"milo v3","date":". 01-20-2016, 06:50 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-20T16:01:53-08:00","id":812977,"title":"","content":"I'm in agreement that tiers are not really that useful for CofD. In nWoD (1e? Do we need to specify that anymore for nWoD?), I ran crossovers. We had a mage. He didn't really outshine anyone else. It was fine.<br /> <br /> That said, debating the merit of tiers seems kind of off-topic for the thread OP started. I kind of wish people wouldn't come into someone's thread just to shout &quot;BADWRONGFUN.&quot;<br /> <br /> So in the spirit of participating rather than just shutting people down, here is my suggestion for Tier metrics:<br /> <br /> 1) Considering an individual that can do everything that the splat can do, how many situations will they have a solution for and to what degree?<br /> 2) Considering an individual straight out of chargen, how many situations will they have a solution for and to what degree?<br /> <br /> Don't need an objective absolute measure. It's about in relation to the others.<br /> <br /> The important thing in tiers is generally the following:<br /> 1) Versatility<br /> 2) Can they do anything better than anyone else/most others<br /> 3) Still mostly versatility","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1692-maina","name":"Maina","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1692_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"724"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-20T16:22:22-08:00","id":812990,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PenDragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/810975-power-tiers-in-2e?p=812966#post812966\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That comment was certainly not directed at you. I'd forgotten you'd brought it up otherwise I'd have noted that. It was, in fact, not directed at anyone. Evolved splat threads tend to spiral into bitter argument, even between normally courteous individuals.<br /> <br /> No harm, no foul.</div> </div> </div> </div>I realize, hence the &quot;I couldn't resist part&quot;. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> Cheers.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.greece-bynight.com\" target=\"_blank\">Greece By Night LARP</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/59-stylanski","name":"stylanski","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar59_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"299"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-20T16:42:18-08:00","id":813011,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maina</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/810975-power-tiers-in-2e?p=812977#post812977\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The important thing in tiers is generally the following:<br /> 1) Versatility<br /> 2) Can they do anything better than anyone else/most others<br /> 3) Still mostly versatility</div> </div> </div> </div>To be fair, this is mostly the metric for D&amp;D 3.5e's tier list as well. As if you need to talk to an entity who speaks an alien language, who do you look to? The Fighter or the Arcanist?<br /> <br /> Heck, the largest damage dealers are by far the mundane characters. I have a character that strikes for more than her own HP each swing.<br /> <br /> <br /> EDIT: Also the person who made the tier list for 3.5e says in essence that the Druid/Wizard/Cleric are fundamentally playing a different game than the Fighter, Rogue, and Ranger.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9830-reshyshira","name":"ReshyShira","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9830_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"589"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-20T17:38:29-08:00","id":813043,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>stylanski</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/810975-power-tiers-in-2e?p=812959#post812959\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You misunderstood me. I don't want Vampires or Werewolves to rival Mages by getting Arch[Insert Splat Here]. In my games, even in crossovers, I give Mages (for example) access only to the creative thaumaturgy system from Blood Sorcery. Lupines often get Protean, Vigor, plus another couple of disciplines depending on the character's background. Similarly, I would run a game of Archmages by giving access to the other splats to the same kind of powers that Mages get.<br /> <br /> I <i>bitch</i> (sorry PenDragon, couldn't resist <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" />) because I like what Mage has done (give the finger to WoD and move on with its life by going ahead and cranking up the power dial for the sake of allowing players and STs to explore more of the universe) and hope that <i>at least</i> the rest of the Three Big Ones (Mage, Werewolf, Vampire) should also have the opportunity to offer that kind of breadth of different levels of play.</div> </div> </div> </div>As mentioned earlier we're getting an elders book for Vampire and since it's been so long since I remember the developer mentioning there is something that is going to touch on methuselas. I haven't kept up on Werewolf so no idea what that team has in plans. Also your post pretty much highlights part of why tiers was dropped. Too many people confuse scope of participation with scope of personal power. There is absolutely NOTHING stopping Vampire, Werewolf, Prometheus,etc stories that involve dealing with entities and situations with cosmic significance. That breathe of levels of play is already there but not all games are going to focus on the same things equally and thinking they would is setting yourself up for disappointment. Focus isn't the same thing as potential.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-20T18:40:33-08:00","id":813077,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ReshyShira</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/810975-power-tiers-in-2e?p=813011#post813011\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <br /> EDIT: Also the person who made the tier list for 3.5e says in essence that the Druid/Wizard/Cleric are fundamentally playing a different game than the Fighter, Rogue, and Ranger.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is due in large part to the absolute lack of any spellcasting of any sort inherent to those classes. Well ranger has some, but its limited, more so than even a paladins.<br /> <br /> No matter how you dice it, access to a decent spell list is a massive agency boon, because it gives you options to work with that are simply more than move and attack. Or making a skillcheck<br /> <br /> CofD, due to everyone except mortals having access to a degree of supernatural power, faces a very mitigated and reduced version of this problem. Because everyone has their own magical unfairnes, it's very much like comparing the merits of oracles and sorcerers against clerics and wizards...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/607039-homebrew-mechs-walkers-ect\" target=\"_blank\">Mechs:</a> Because even the Chronicles of Darkness needs robot fights.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/813387-darkframe-a-far-future-crossover-setting\" target=\"_blank\">DarkFrame</a>: Crossover setting that puts Chronicles of Darkness in the far future that is Warframe.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless\" target=\"_blank\">Monarch: The Endless</a> You are an alien ruler, charged with maintaining a people who you shape to suit your needs.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7015-almarck","name":"Almarck","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-20T18:48:00-08:00","id":813082,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Almarck</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/810975-power-tiers-in-2e?p=813077#post813077\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This is due in large part to the absolute lack of any spellcasting of any sort inherent to those classes. Well ranger has some, but its limited, more so than even a paladins.<br /> <br /> No matter how you dice it, access to a decent spell list is a massive agency boon, because it gives you options to work with that are simply more than move and attack. Or making a skillcheck<br /> <br /> CofD, due to everyone except mortals having access to a degree of supernatural power, faces a very mitigated and reduced version of this problem. Because everyone has their own magical unfairnes, it's very much like comparing the merits of oracles and sorcerers against clerics and wizards...</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Actually Ranger is pretty awesome once you take off all the awful bits. They can get Wild Shape, Wizard casting up to 5ths, along with full BaB and two good saves, and a d8 hit die.<br /> <br /> <br /> Also yes I agree that the power difference isn't as vast. However, a lot of it comes down to resources. In a pinch a Mage can improvise, for most other supernaturals if they don't got the right power they have no real ability to improvise. If mages were constrained solely to Rotes they'd lose a good deal of their versatility. They'd still be quite powerful, mind. However, they'd suffer the lack of flexibility that other Splats tend to have.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9830-reshyshira","name":"ReshyShira","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9830_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"589"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-20T20:45:33-08:00","id":813147,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Almarck</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/810975-power-tiers-in-2e?p=813077#post813077\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">CofD, due to everyone except mortals having access to a degree of supernatural power, faces a very mitigated and reduced version of this problem. Because everyone has their own magical unfairnes, it's very much like comparing the merits of oracles and sorcerers against clerics and wizards...</div> </div> </div> </div>In 3/.5e Clerics and Wizards were demonstrably more capable than Favored Souls (what I assume you meant by Oracle) and Sorcerers due to their access to a greater list of spells.<br /> <br /> Which is where the &quot;power&quot; of Mage comes in: Creative Thaumaturgy coupled with having only ten specializations that manage to cover all of everything gives a <i>lot</i> of versatility. A Mage with Mind 5 can do <i>orders of magnitude more </i>than a Vampire with both Dominate 5 and Majesty 5 for half the investment.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1452235-proin-s-legacy-hub\" target=\"_blank\">proin's Legacy hub</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2757-proindrakenzol","name":"proindrakenzol","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1514"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-20T21:10:03-08:00","id":813156,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>proindrakenzol</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/810975-power-tiers-in-2e?p=813147#post813147\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> In 3/.5e Clerics and Wizards were demonstrably more capable than Favored Souls (what I assume you meant by Oracle) and Sorcerers due to their access to a greater list of spells.<br /> <br /> Which is where the &quot;power&quot; of Mage comes in: Creative Thaumaturgy coupled with having only ten specializations that manage to cover all of everything gives a <i>lot</i> of versatility. A Mage with Mind 5 can do <i>orders of magnitude more </i>than a Vampire with both Dominate 5 and Majesty 5 for half the investment.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> No, I meant Oracles.<br /> I play Pathfinder on ocassion.<br /> <br /> Oracles were very improved over the Favored Soul due to the breadth of options given to them in a variety of themes. Sorcerer actually gets class features good enough that you may never take a Prestige class.<br /> <br /> Spontaneous Casters in Pathfinder do not have the benefits of free choice casting like a Prepared caster. However, they get better specialization options and are arguably more &quot;fun&quot; to play.<br /> <br /> <br /> I'm certain there's cons to the Mind 5 over Dominator or Majesty route. But I am not so certain as I don't play mage or have experiance with mindhacking at all. I don't know how well or how easy it is for a Mind 5 Master in the current rulesdraft","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/607039-homebrew-mechs-walkers-ect\" target=\"_blank\">Mechs:</a> Because even the Chronicles of Darkness needs robot fights.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/813387-darkframe-a-far-future-crossover-setting\" target=\"_blank\">DarkFrame</a>: Crossover setting that puts Chronicles of Darkness in the far future that is Warframe.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless\" target=\"_blank\">Monarch: The Endless</a> You are an alien ruler, charged with maintaining a people who you shape to suit your needs.","edited":{"userid":7015,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7015-almarck","user":"Almarck","date":". 01-21-2016, 12:15 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7015-almarck","name":"Almarck","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-20T21:24:00-08:00","id":813161,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>proindrakenzol</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/810975-power-tiers-in-2e?p=813147#post813147\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> In 3/.5e Clerics and Wizards were demonstrably more capable than Favored Souls (what I assume you meant by Oracle) and Sorcerers due to their access to a greater list of spells.<br /> <br /> Which is where the &quot;power&quot; of Mage comes in: Creative Thaumaturgy coupled with having only ten specializations that manage to cover all of everything gives a <i>lot</i> of versatility. A Mage with Mind 5 can do <i>orders of magnitude more </i>than a Vampire with both Dominate 5 and Majesty 5 for half the investment.</div> </div> </div> </div>On the flip side, a single dot of Dominate or Majesty can do far more than a single dot in Mind, if memory serves.<br /> <br /> This is why I suggested using characters straight from chargen as one of the metrics.<br /> <br /> A Ventrue straight out of chargen would be better at mind control than a Mastigos (if I remember right) straight out of chargen. Though yeah, that flips later on.<br /> <br /> I feel like this gives a better judge of potency, since this is closer to the mode average for what a member of the splat is capable of.<br /> <br /> The theoretical member of a splat that can do everything at once has always been my biggest frustration in Storyteller tier lists and white room.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1692-maina","name":"Maina","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1692_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"724"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-20T21:33:35-08:00","id":813165,"title":"","content":"As far as 1e was concerned, Mages couldn't straight up mind control until Mind 4, a dot higher than they could manage at character creation. They could do a lot of other things, like grant themselves social/mental skills/attributes and make anyone with less resolve than potency of a certain spell unable to harm them, but mind control was one of the big things that wasn't quite in range of a starting character.<br /> <br /> 2e of course is going to mix all of this around quite a bit. I want to say that mind control in 2e was stated as being Ruling, which is 2 dots.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2309-ashenrogue","name":"Ashenrogue","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1388"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-20T21:39:16-08:00","id":813170,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ashenrogue</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/810975-power-tiers-in-2e?p=813165#post813165\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">2e of course is going to mix all of this around quite a bit. I want to say that mind control in 2e was stated as being Ruling, which is 2 dots.</div> </div> </div> </div>From the Devblog:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <ul><li><b>Ruling</b> spells grant fuller control over phenomena than a mere Compelling spell. Water can be made to flow uphill or into unnatural shapes (Matter), <b>animals (or even human beings) can be commanded (Life or Mind)</b>, or time can be momentarily made to accelerate or slow down (Time). A Ruling spell can\u2019t fundamentally alter its subject\u2019s abilities: Water can be directed, but not turned solid or gaseous. Time can be altered, but not overwritten. An animal can be commanded, but not made stronger or fiercer.</li> </ul> </div> </div> </div><br /> Emphasis mine.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1452235-proin-s-legacy-hub\" target=\"_blank\">proin's Legacy hub</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2757-proindrakenzol","name":"proindrakenzol","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1514"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-20T23:05:00-08:00","id":813202,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maina</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/810975-power-tiers-in-2e?p=813161#post813161\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On the flip side, a single dot of Dominate or Majesty can do far more than a single dot in Mind, if memory serves.</div> </div> </div> </div>Pretty close. It's more that a single dot of Dominate or Majesty allows a bit more focused power in that particular arena. Conversely, a single dot of Mind allows less direct power, but a whole lot of effects that can stack up.<br /> <br /> Dominate 1 lets you command a person. At Dominate 5, you can possess a victim's body, reshape someone's memories, implant suggestions bolstered by other Dominate powers, and completely control someone's actions.<br /> <br /> Majesty 1 lets you awe everyone around you, gaining bonuses to most any social engagement as well as suffering few, if any, penalties.<br /> <br /> Mind 1 lets you, among other things: learn a character's emotions, Aspirations, Mental and Social Attributes, glean insight into the target's true nature and thoughts, put eidetic memory to shame. You also have access to Mind Mage Sight. You can't dominate another mind at this point. Mind 2, however, lets you do so, and with Reach, you can even force a subject to execute suicidal commands. At Mind 5, the mage can also possess people, create a self-aware intelligence from nothing, permanently erase someone's memories (including selective erasure), trap someone in a thought loop, completely rewrite personalities, grant Skills, induce hallucinations, cripple a target's mental faculties, instantly understand any language, create telepathic links both deep and shallow, etc. Lots more on top of all that.<br /> <br /> So a single dot in most Disciplines typically provides more focused ability in a given area, often accompanied by a greater ease in accomplishing an action. For a mage, bodily merging with soil or stone or concrete is a pretty complex spell. For a vampire, it's a simple application of Protean 1, done as an instant action! A single dot of, say, Life doesn't allow you to change your form so radically, but it provides a wealth of benefits that Unmarked Grave cannot. However, to get the most out of her spells, a mage must make use of Reach, and that brings with it risks. Magical backfires are potentially far worse than just a fizzled spell in the face of an angry vampire.<br /> <br /> Really, any tier list would have to account for so much data that it's difficult to determine anything concrete. Tier lists in fighting games work because although every fighter has a different style and moveset, they're all being measured by the same activity: a fight. Everyone has frame data and damage and other attributes. Everyone interacts with the same base engine. There's a lot of common ground in the Chronicles, but not every character type is built to do the same things. That is, they're not built to interact with the basic engine in the same way. A mage can shapeshift or talk to spirits, but she's coming at it in a completely different way than a werewolf.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Freelancer </b>\u2022 Available for work!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/109-claire-redfield","name":"Claire Redfield","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar109_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"672"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-21T06:03:56-08:00","id":813312,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ShadowKnight1224</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/810975-power-tiers-in-2e?p=812663#post812663\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> But clearly this is a very sensitive matter to you, so I won't push it any further.</div> </div> </div> </div> Don't assume anything about me, its offensive.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>stylanski</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/810975-power-tiers-in-2e?p=812775#post812775\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I want my Requiem chronicle through the ages, dammit! Legalize Methuselahs already! :'( <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div> I actually adapted Sothesis Ascend rules for that. That's one downside to the &quot;infinite monsters&quot; thing the CofD does. The core games get diluted when someone else grabs their stuff, so less books come out about vampires seeking Golconda, or dealing with the underworld, or games through the ages.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PenDragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/810975-power-tiers-in-2e?p=812786#post812786\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A and the (supposedly) tragic absence of Arch[Insert Splat Here]s.</div> </div> </div> </div> It IS tragic. I want my Unchained archdemons! *throws a temper tantrum*<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>milo v3</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/810975-power-tiers-in-2e?p=812899#post812899\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well if you go off D&amp;D/PF style tiers, then yes Obfuscate is much much much worse than the mind arcana. Because it is much less versatile and each dot of obfuscate is very specific in it's abilities while the Mind Arcana can accomplish the same stuff as Obfuscate and more in general because of how you can use the Mind Arcana to do anything related to the mind rather than just obscure things.</div> </div> </div> </div> Only if you ignore opertunity costs. People forget minor things like Spell Tolerance and Limits. A mage can only prepare so many spells at once, and a good chunk of magic can't be cast as an instant spell. Meanwhile, a vampire is ready for whatever they need to do -immediately-. That's something even D&amp;D tiers take into account.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>milo v3</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/810975-power-tiers-in-2e?p=812948#post812948\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do you realize one of the themes of both Mage and Demon are &quot;Okay we can do basically anything, but can we risk doing it?&quot; and another is &quot;Okay we can do basically anything, but is it ethical to do so?&quot; right..... Their themes want them to be high tier....</div> </div> </div> </div> People put too much stock in that. Mages and demons can do anything... in theory. The reality is that they can't. In theory, I could become President, get a PhD in astrophysics, and run the Boston Marathon. The reality is that its not happening. And not just because of &quot;its unethical.&quot; There's sharp limits on what mages can do at once. Mages, as a whole, can do anything. Individual mages are much more limited in what they can acomplish. Same holds true with demons - there's sharp limits on what potential they can fulfill. <br /> <br /> I mean, lets be honest. If you're going by just &quot;do anything!&quot; than vampires and werewolves can potentially do anything with their sorceries and spirit rites as well, and Changelings could theoretically pull off anything with the right Contract or goblin vow. That's &quot;top tier&quot; for everyone if we want to go with the raw potential of the different splats and no drawbacks or limits. If you want to get into rating something, you do have to take those pesky opertunity costs and drawbacks into account.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maina</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/810975-power-tiers-in-2e?p=812977#post812977\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That said, debating the merit of tiers seems kind of off-topic for the thread OP started.</div> </div> </div> </div> I gave my answer, and the answer was &quot;everyone's roughly equal.&quot; Write out your answers. Make a list. Don't just give metrics, give an actual list of ratings and why.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>proindrakenzol</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/810975-power-tiers-in-2e?p=813147#post813147\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Which is where the &quot;power&quot; of Mage comes in: Creative Thaumaturgy coupled with having only ten specializations that manage to cover all of everything gives a <i>lot</i> of versatility. A Mage with Mind 5 can do <i>orders of magnitude more </i>than a Vampire with both Dominate 5 and Majesty 5 for half the investment.</div> </div> </div> </div> Not in 2e. So far, from what we've seen, a mage needs Mind 4 to open all Doors in a Social Maneuvering effect. That's still limited by what a normal person would agree to with a social maneuvering check - there are things he would still say no to. A vampire with Dominate 1 or Majesty 2 bypasses the social maneuvering and move right to &quot;do what I say,you don't get the option to say no.&quot; Furthermore, its been a while since I looked, but I'm fairly sure that you can't cast that spell on demand either - you need some time to prep it. That's a rather notable drawback that limits versatility. <br /> <br /> That's the problem with mage theory crafting. It sounds good in a white room, but in reality of playing, it doesn't quite work out that way.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>proindrakenzol</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/810975-power-tiers-in-2e?p=813170#post813170\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">From the Devblog:<br /> Emphasis mine.</div> </div> </div> </div> On the other hand, we've got one sample Mind 4 spell that relates to controlling others. I somehow doubt that opening Doors is a high level effect when outright mind control is a lower level. We really need to get the entire book before we definitely say anything about 2e powers. <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Claire Redfield</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/810975-power-tiers-in-2e?p=813202#post813202\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Majesty 1 lets you awe everyone around you, gaining bonuses to most any social engagement as well as suffering few, if any, penalties.</div> </div> </div> </div> Majesty 1 negates all penalties, though not Impressions. Also, much more notably, Awe completely negates the penalty from being low Humanity. A Nosferatu with Majesty 1 effectively suffers no clan bane while its active, and both Majesty and Nightmare key off the same attributes (Pres, Manip) and skill (Empathy for both). That's kind of handy to have.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-21T06:23:37-08:00","id":813324,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/810975-power-tiers-in-2e?p=813312#post813312\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Don't assume anything about me, its offensive.</div> </div> </div> </div>You're acting overly sensitive about the subject so it's a logical conclusion to come to. If you're feeling offended by the comment, I feel it's more because you choose to feel offended than the comment inherently being offensive in and of itself.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2309-ashenrogue","name":"Ashenrogue","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1388"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-21T06:35:30-08:00","id":813331,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/810975-power-tiers-in-2e?p=813312#post813312\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> People put too much stock in that. Mages and demons can do anything... in theory. The reality is that they can't. In theory, I could become President, get a PhD in astrophysics, and run the Boston Marathon. The reality is that its not happening. And not just because of &quot;its unethical.&quot; There's sharp limits on what mages can do at once. Mages, as a whole, can do anything. Individual mages are much more limited in what they can acomplish. Same holds true with demons - there's sharp limits on what potential they can fulfill.<br /> <br /> I mean, lets be honest. If you're going by just &quot;do anything!&quot; than vampires and werewolves can potentially do anything with their sorceries and spirit rites as well, and Changelings could theoretically pull off anything with the right Contract or goblin vow. That's &quot;top tier&quot; for everyone if we want to go with the raw potential of the different splats and no drawbacks or limits. If you want to get into rating something, you do have to take those pesky opertunity costs and drawbacks into account.</div> </div> </div> </div>Except one is &quot;okay, my character has five dots in dominate so he can do a small number of specifics thing with minds very well&quot; and the other is &quot;okay, my character has five dots in the Mind Arcana, so he can do anything he wants with minds.&quot; Some groups have very specific sets of powers, like vampires. While mages are much more versatile and can do many more things. They are not necessarily stronger, simply more versatile, and in roleplaying games applicable versatility is generally the most direct form of power.<br /> <br /> I'm not saying one character can do Everything. I'm saying that individuals in some splats can do more than the others.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":8331,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","user":"milo v3","date":". 01-21-2016, 10:04 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-21T06:49:43-08:00","id":813338,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/810975-power-tiers-in-2e?p=813312#post813312\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">People forget minor things like Spell Tolerance and Limits. A mage can only prepare so many spells at once, and a good chunk of magic can't be cast as an instant spell.</div> </div> </div> </div>Spell tolerance isn't a thing in 2e. Spell control is limited only by paradox, and everything can be cast at instant speed for one reach.<br /> <br /> So the reason that everyone forgets these limits is that they no longer exist.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-21T07:07:23-08:00","id":813350,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ashenrogue</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/810975-power-tiers-in-2e?p=813324#post813324\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You're acting overly sensitive about the subject so it's a logical conclusion to come to. If you're feeling offended by the comment, I feel it's more because you choose to feel offended than the comment inherently being offensive in and of itself.</div> </div> </div> </div> Its rude to assume things about people feelings through text; that way leads to personal attacks, and I don't care for it. And I do choose to be offended by what looks like a passive-aggressive attack in order to deflect not answering a question.<br /> <br /> I'm noticing a trend. Only the people who've actually said they don't like tiers have bothered to put together an actual list of any kind. Hells, I even made a list. Shadowknight, you, any of the others who want a tier list haven't even tried to make one. I make a challenge to do so, and get called &quot;overly sensitive.&quot; What &quot;logical conclusions&quot; should I be making about that, pray tell?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>milo v3</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/810975-power-tiers-in-2e?p=813331#post813331\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">From what I've seen it's not that hard to do improvised spells in magic...</div> </div> </div> </div> Come up with? No, not hard. Actually USE them in the course of play on the fly? That's another matter entirely. Mages can, in theory, do a lot of things. But, like I said, there are limits in place that prevent them from being able to cast all those spells in game. Let alone the assumption that you can do all of them as Instant Actions. There are a significant number of spells that are cast only as rituals.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Except one is &quot;okay, my character has five dots in dominate so he can do a small number of specifics thing with minds very well&quot; and the other is &quot;okay, my character has five dots in the Mind Arcana, so he can do anything he wants with minds.&quot; Some groups have very specific sets of powers, like vampires. While mages are much more versatile and can do many more things. They are not necessarily stronger, simply more versatile, and in roleplaying games applicable versatility is generally the most direct form of power. </div> </div> </div> Except that the mage can't do whatever he wants to do with minds. Versatility is only a &quot;direct form of power&quot; when you can actually apply it in game. Potential != actual ability. Situations aren't always that flexible for a mage. That's the whole point I'm making. You're assuming the mage has idealized circumstances to cast these spells, when that doesn't happen so much in play. Many spells require far more time than it takes to snap off a Discipline, Gift, Contract, or psychic ability. I'm assuming that the limits on active spells at once and tolerance remain in 2e as well.<br /> <br /> Assuming that someone with Mind 5 can vanish as easily as a vampire with Obfscate 1, mind control as easily as Dominate 1, charm as easily as Majesty 1, and create hallucinations as easily as Nightmare 1, plus having a Mage Shield and Mage Sight up is simply not going to happen in game without seriously crippling your mage in other ways. Assuming he can do this as fast (a large number of spells take more than a single round to cast) or easily (vampires seem to have advantage when it comes to dice pools, it seems) as a vampire is also not a given. Vampires are also immune to mind control when riding the wave, something mages can't repeat.<br /> <br /> You used the phrase &quot;applicable versatility.&quot; I'm arguing that the &quot;applicable&quot; part should not be assumed with mages. I've seen any number of games where it has not held true.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2102,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","user":"MCN","date":". 01-21-2016, 10:09 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-21T07:18:22-08:00","id":813351,"title":"","content":"Mage sight and mage shield are an intrinsic power and an attainment, respectively. <br /> <br /> Look, your assessment is very well reasoned, but it's based entirely on limitations we <i>know</i> don't exist in second edition. Not one of your points is going to hold true.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-21T07:18:34-08:00","id":813352,"title":"","content":"I think the fundamental concept people are getting at is that some power sets are inherently more flexible than others. Nothing terrible controversial there and we've seen with blood magic supplements that varying models of flexibility is possible as well. Likewise if memory serves, I apologize as it's been a bit since I've looked at W:tf 2e. Gifts or at least a few gained more flexibility with 2e. Inherent flexibility varies depending on how the mechanics are set while potential of any individual character using that flexibility varies as well. But the fundamental concept that some powers sets are more flexible than others still holds true.<br /> <br /> I don't think there is anything terribly fruitful with people sniping at each other over the minutia you can find within all that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-21T07:23:51-08:00","id":813356,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/810975-power-tiers-in-2e?p=813350#post813350\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Its rude to assume things about people feelings through text; that way leads to personal attacks, and I don't care for it. And I do choose to be offended by what looks like a passive-aggressive attack in order to deflect not answering a question.<br /> <br /> I'm noticing a trend. Only the people who've actually said they don't like tiers have bothered to put together an actual list of any kind. Hells, I even made a list. Shadowknight, you, any of the others who want a tier list haven't even tried to make one. I make a challenge to do so, and get called &quot;overly sensitive.&quot; What &quot;logical conclusions&quot; should I be making about that, pray tell?<br /> <br /> Come up with? No, not hard. Actually USE them in the course of play on the fly? That's another matter entirely. Mages can, in theory, do a lot of things. But, like I said, there are limits in place that prevent them from being able to cast all those spells in game. Let alone the assumption that you can do all of them as Instant Actions. There are a significant number of spells that are cast only as rituals.<br /> <br /> Except that the mage can't do whatever he wants to do with minds. Versatility is only a &quot;direct form of power&quot; when you can actually apply it in game. Potential != actual ability. Situations aren't always that flexible for a mage. That's the whole point I'm making. You're assuming the mage has idealized circumstances to cast these spells, when that doesn't happen so much in play. Many spells require far more time than it takes to snap off a Discipline, Gift, Contract, or psychic ability. I'm assuming that the limits on active spells at once and tolerance remain in 2e as well.<br /> <br /> Assuming that someone with Mind 5 can vanish as easily as a vampire with Obfscate 1, mind control as easily as Dominate 1, charm as easily as Majesty 1, and create hallucinations as easily as Nightmare 1, plus having a Mage Shield and Mage Sight up is simply not going to happen in game without seriously crippling your mage in other ways. Assuming he can do this as fast (a large number of spells take more than a single round to cast) or easily (vampires seem to have advantage when it comes to dice pools, it seems) as a vampire is also not a given. Vampires are also immune to mind control when riding the wave, something mages can't repeat.<br /> <br /> You used the phrase &quot;applicable versatility.&quot; I'm arguing that the &quot;applicable&quot; part should not be assumed with mages. I've seen any number of games where it has not held true.</div> </div> </div> </div>1. Several of the issues your stating are going to be removed in 2e.<br /> 2. Those issues don't really even matter since it doesn't change the fact those things just make it slightly harder to do the things. With a bit of prep you Can do anything mind-powery with mind 5. Yes, vampire's disciplines can be much more efficient at doing singular specific things. But that's all those specific singular things can do, which is why they are highly efficient.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-21T07:31:27-08:00","id":813358,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/810975-power-tiers-in-2e?p=813312#post813312\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A Nosferatu with Majesty 1 effectively suffers no clan bane while its active,</div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"font-size:12px\">That is false</span><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">. &quot;For the rest of the scene, he suffers no penalties to Social rolls from his actions or appearance </span>&quot;. Your clan bane is not your actions or appearance, it's a supernatural force, which reduces your humanity by two in terms of humanity penalties and downgrades rolls. <br /> <br /> Hence, Majesty helps to fail less and offset the penalties (since you're likely to get - from humanity), but it does not outright remove the bane. Just helps fight it. </span></span><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B5_EJSgV1u4SOFFJc3M5VmFDWVk?resourcekey=0-GEErNnDbGqlKYgoiuGausw&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Bloodline conversions</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1IbeKfqhWuG8jPN9vpGmDo0VY9n9-4ejxvRzfJRoir4k/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My House rules</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/294-griautis","name":"Griautis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar294_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-21T07:37:04-08:00","id":813361,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>milo v3</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/810975-power-tiers-in-2e?p=813356#post813356\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">1. Several of the issues your stating are going to be removed in 2e.<br /> 2. Those issues don't really even matter since it doesn't change the fact those things just make it slightly harder to do the things. With a bit of prep you Can do anything mind-powery with mind 5. Yes, vampire's disciplines can be much more efficient at doing singular specific things. But that's all those specific singular things can do, which is why they are highly efficient.</div> </div> </div> </div> 1) Which issues, where does it say it, because I have not seen it.<br /> <br /> 2) &quot;With a little bit of prep.&quot; Mage powers are all about needing the proper preparation. That's a drawback, because if you don't prepare, and you're not given the time to prepare, they're not applicable. And that time needed to prepare very often turns out to not be little. Only in context-free white rooms do we have all the time and knowledge and yantra to do that &quot;little bit of prep.&quot; I don't agree with handwaving away any of actual drawbacks of Awakened magic here, and we haven't even touched on the new paradox yet.<br /> <br /> And I'd like to also mention that you're kind of underplaying Disicplines as well. Dominate 1 covers at the effects of least two different Mind spells, maybe three. That's more than &quot;specific singular thing.&quot; Disciplines do have an amount of flexibility to them, plus there's Devotions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2102,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","user":"MCN","date":". 01-21-2016, 10:44 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-21T07:45:31-08:00","id":813366,"title":"","content":"Blogs, developer comments... Dave's basically walked off with the foundation of your arguments in a wheelbarrow.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-21T08:02:30-08:00","id":813376,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Griautis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/810975-power-tiers-in-2e?p=813358#post813358\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\">That is false</span><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">. &quot;For the rest of the scene, he suffers no penalties to Social rolls from his actions or appearance </span>&quot;. Your clan bane is not your actions or appearance, it's a supernatural force, which reduces your humanity by two in terms of humanity penalties and downgrades rolls.<br /> <br /> Hence, Majesty helps to fail less and offset the penalties (since you're likely to get - from humanity), but it does not outright remove the bane. Just helps fight it. </span></span></div> </div> </div> </div> Majesty effectively negates the Humanity penalties; the Humanity scale describes the penalties in terms of appearing sick and deathly, and as you quoted, someone using Majesty suffers no penalties from appearance. The Nosferatu bane only makes Humanity penalties worse. Its still a Humanity-based penalty, and thus appearance based, though.<br /> <br /> Though, I am incorrect in two regards. Lower Humanity also makes it harder to make Empathy checks, which is not covered by Majesty. And I forgot the Presence/Manipulation failures to dramatic failures part - I only remembered the Humanity as two dots lower bit. Granted, most Nosferatu I've seen played have a high enough Presence and Manipulation score for Nightmare to work, so its rare for them to fail those rolls in the first place; I can't think of any time that came up.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2102,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","user":"MCN","date":". 01-21-2016, 11:05 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-21T08:49:02-08:00","id":813401,"title":"","content":"Humanity penalties are for relating to humans because you are less human yourself. The appearance is just fluff, I assume for when Blush of Life isn't active.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> These modifiers<br /> apply to rolls relating to humans. Manipulating humans for<br /> food with Subterfuge or frightening them with Intimidation<br /> are not affected; but trying to understand a human\u2019s emotional<br /> cues with the Empathy Skill would be affected. </div> </div> </div>One might assume that an appearance-based malus would affect all social rolls except maybe Intimidation. This seems explicitly geared towards comprehending human behavior.<br /> <br /> Which kind of makes the Nosferatu Clan Bane not make a lot of sense, but what can you do?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1692-maina","name":"Maina","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1692_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"724"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-21T08:58:36-08:00","id":813409,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maina</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/810975-power-tiers-in-2e?p=813401#post813401\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Humanity penalties are for relating to humans because you are less human yourself. The appearance is just fluff, I assume for when Blush of Life isn't active.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> One might assume that an appearance-based malus would affect all social rolls except maybe Intimidation. This seems explicitly geared towards comprehending human behavior.<br /> <br /> Which kind of makes the Nosferatu Clan Bane not make a lot of sense, but what can you do?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> so at best, Majesty removes the -2 Humanity from Nosferatu bane, assume'ing that the Nosferatu's particular bane is appearance based?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B5_EJSgV1u4SOFFJc3M5VmFDWVk?resourcekey=0-GEErNnDbGqlKYgoiuGausw&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Bloodline conversions</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1IbeKfqhWuG8jPN9vpGmDo0VY9n9-4ejxvRzfJRoir4k/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My House rules</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/294-griautis","name":"Griautis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar294_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-21T09:11:54-08:00","id":813418,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/810975-power-tiers-in-2e?p=813350#post813350\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Its rude to assume things about people feelings through text; that way leads to personal attacks, and I don't care for it. And I do choose to be offended by what looks like a passive-aggressive attack in order to deflect not answering a question.<br /> <br /> I'm noticing a trend. Only the people who've actually said they don't like tiers have bothered to put together an actual list of any kind. Hells, I even made a list. Shadowknight, you, any of the others who want a tier list haven't even tried to make one. I make a challenge to do so, and get called &quot;overly sensitive.&quot; What &quot;logical conclusions&quot; should I be making about that, pray tell?</div> </div> </div> </div>A lot can be gleaned from a person through text believe it or not. While, like any other method of detecting emotional states (unless someone has some sort of magic power in real life that flawlessly lets them know such things), it isn't perfectly accurate. It isn't inherently rude to make assumptions based off of such things anymore than it is rude to assume someone who's crying might be upset about something.<br /> <br /> Long story short, writing carries tones, and the tone of your writing (at least in this thread) has been sharp, somewhat condescending, and just a tad bit hostile. I'm not sure if you don't realize you're doing it or if I might just be misreading/imagining things, but so far you have clearly come off as sensitive regarding this subject matter. To be frank, to me you act like tier lists shot your dog or something. Now I apologize if that isn't what you were intending, but at least to me, that's how you've been coming off.<br /> <br /> Now, as for creating tier lists in this thread goes, the reason I haven't attempted to do so is incredibly simple actually. Mage 2e isn't out yet. Mage is one of the big 3, and I personally wouldn't feel right making a tier list without at least the core book for the main 3 lines being out and available. Yes, we know a lot about mage through spoilers revealed over the course of its development, but we don't know everything. I'm definitely waiting for that to release before attempting to construct any sort of tier list.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2309,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2309-ashenrogue","user":"Ashenrogue","date":". 01-21-2016, 12:21 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2309-ashenrogue","name":"Ashenrogue","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1388"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-21T09:16:51-08:00","id":813420,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ashenrogue</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/810975-power-tiers-in-2e?p=813418#post813418\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A lot can be gleaned from a person through text believe it or not. While, like any other method of detecting emotional states (unless someone has some sort of magic in real life that flawlessly lets them know such things), it isn't perfectly accurate, it isn't inherently rude to make assumptions based off of such things anymore than it is rude to assume someone who's crying might be upset about something.<br /> <br /> Long story short, writing carries tones, and the tone of your writing (at least in this thread) has been sharp, somewhat condescending, and just a tad bit hostile. I'm not sure if you don't realize you're doing it or if I might just be misreading/imagining things, but so far you have clearly come off as sensitive regarding this subject matter. To be frank, to me you act like tier lists shot your dog or something. Now I apologize if that isn't what you were intending, but at least to me, that's how you've been coming off.<br /> <br /> Now, as for creating tier lists in this thread goes, the reason I haven't attempted to do so is incredibly simple actually. Mage 2e isn't out yet. Mage is one of the big 3, and I personally wouldn't feel right making a tier list without at least the core book for the main 3 lines being out and available. Yes, we know a lot about mage through spoilers revealed over the course of its development, but we don't know everything. I'm definitely waiting for that to release before attempting to construct any sort of tier list.</div> </div> </div> </div> In addition I would say this thread also shows us that &quot;tier list&quot; as a concept can cover a wide variety of different things. So not all tier lists are going to tier things based on the same criteria. I don't think there's anything particularly positive about demanding people conjure up any particular type. Particularly when far too often people take tiered concepts less as the guidelines and outlines they are meant to be and attempt to insert rigid definitions and separations with them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-21T10:15:15-08:00","id":813462,"title":"","content":"What is the criteria for 'power?'<br /> <br /> I've only skimmed, but so far have seen someone mentioning being able to engulf entire cities in flame, but that was dismissed as not versatile enough. Meanwhile this last page seems to be arguing over a modifier of 2 in regards to social rolls.<br /> <br /> No one really seemed to follow up with the obvious. Influence allows one to Strengthen, Control, Manipulate, Create and Mass Create the subject of its Influence.<br /> <br /> There is Influence for everything. Every concept, every emotion, every element, nearly every object created, nearly everything that was alive or still is. The only thing that doesn't have a spirit is humans. And they are influenced by Life, by Emotion, by Thought and Dream, Blood and Pain, Slavery or Freedom, all of which can have corresponding Influences somewhere or another, which can then find their way into the hands of werewolves, through fetish or gift or rite.<br /> <br /> Plus while the idea of 'tracking' was glossed over, no one bothered to point out between a variety of werewolf abilities you can basically see a character's entire sheet. Almost everything a character is can be accessed by the werewolf through gifts.<br /> <br /> And a vampire is forced to sleep during the daylight. They are only capable of acting at their full ability once the sun is down. Does this have a bearing on lack of versatility? On their 'power?'","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 01-21-2016, 01:25 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-21T11:11:49-08:00","id":813502,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/810975-power-tiers-in-2e?p=813462#post813462\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What is the criteria for 'power?'<br /> <br /> I've only skimmed, but so far have seen someone mentioning being able to engulf entire cities in flame, but that was dismissed as not versatile enough. Meanwhile this last page seems to be arguing over a modifier of 2 in regards to social rolls.<br /> <br /> No one really seemed to follow up with the obvious. Influence allows one to Strengthen, Control, Manipulate, Create and Mass Create the subject of its Influence.<br /> <br /> There is Influence for everything. Every concept, every emotion, every element, nearly every object created, nearly everything that was alive or still is. The only thing that doesn't have a spirit is humans. And they are influenced by Life, by Emotion, by Thought and Dream, Blood and Pain, Slavery or Freedom, all of which can have corresponding Influences somewhere or another, which can then find their way into the hands of werewolves, through fetish or gift or rite.<br /> <br /> Plus while the idea of 'tracking' was glossed over, no one bothered to point out between a variety of werewolf abilities you can basically see a character's entire sheet. Almost everything a character is can be accessed by the werewolf through gifts.<br /> <br /> And a vampire is forced to sleep during the daylight. They are only capable of acting at their full ability once the sun is down. Does this have a bearing on lack of versatility? On their 'power?'</div> </div> </div> </div>I think versatility is the key metric. Heck in 3.5e casters were the worst damage dealers. Costly and lacking in punch. However they had flexibility, need a curse broken? The wizard can do that. Need to get somewhere fast with short notice? The wizard prepared teleport just in case this happened. Need to talk to an alien intelligence that speaks in images? The wizard can translate that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9830-reshyshira","name":"ReshyShira","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9830_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"589"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-23T14:36:38-08:00","id":815038,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/810975-power-tiers-in-2e?p=813312#post813312\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">People put too much stock in that. Mages and demons can do anything... in theory. The reality is that they can't. In theory, I could become President, get a PhD in astrophysics, and run the Boston Marathon. The reality is that its not happening. And not just because of &quot;its unethical.&quot; There's sharp limits on what mages can do at once. Mages, as a whole, can do anything. Individual mages are much more limited in what they can acomplish. Same holds true with demons - there's sharp limits on what potential they can fulfill.</div> </div> </div> </div>The way I usually put it is Mages can do anything, but they can't do everything.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6748-michael-kenner","name":"Michael Kenner","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6748_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"380"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-23T14:46:37-08:00","id":815049,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/810975-power-tiers-in-2e?p=813366#post813366\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Blogs, developer comments... Dave's basically walked off with the foundation of your arguments in a wheelbarrow.</div> </div> </div> </div>He can have the arguments, a wheelbarrow and anything else he likes once I get that book in my hands (or more accurately that PDF in my kindle).<br /> <br /> Though if the book does say that Mages now do everything, with no limitations whatsoever and have no challenges (which strangely is what people seem to be arguing here), that book is getting deleted.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6748-michael-kenner","name":"Michael Kenner","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6748_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"380"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-23T15:34:30-08:00","id":815077,"title":"","content":"How... how does anything we've said suggest that? And why did you quote me, I wasn't even talking to you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-23T15:35:35-08:00","id":815078,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael Kenner</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/810975-power-tiers-in-2e?p=815049#post815049\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> He can have the arguments, a wheelbarrow and anything else he likes once I get that book in my hands (or more accurately that PDF in my kindle).<br /> <br /> Though if the book does say that Mages now do everything, with no limitations whatsoever and have no challenges (which strangely is what people seem to be arguing here), that book is getting deleted.</div> </div> </div> </div>Probably a good thing then that David Brookshaw isn't anywhere near the sort of developer that the above strawman would apply to. And in the interest of making sure these forums remain a place that writers and developers can interact harmoniously with the fanbase. Maybe we shouldn't toss out these sort of things.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2997,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/","user":"Guest","date":". 01-23-2016, 06:37 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-23T15:50:07-08:00","id":815084,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TyrannicalRabbit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/810975-power-tiers-in-2e?p=815078#post815078\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Probably a good thing then that David Brookshaw isn't anywhere near the sort of developer that the above strawman would apply to. And in the interest of making sure these forums remain a place that writers and developers can interact harmoniously with the fanbase. Maybe we shouldn't toss out these sort of things.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm sorry, I think some element of my tone got lost in putting this to text. That's always the risk to being unnecessarily snarky and I should take more care to avoid that.<br /> <br /> I was expressing how strange it was that people seemed to think that he would take all limitations out of Mage because that's what people seemed to be arguing on this thread previously. That absurd idea of a game without any limits isn't what I expect Dave to release, it's what people seemed to be describing, utterly mystifying me.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6748-michael-kenner","name":"Michael Kenner","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6748_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"380"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-23T16:00:26-08:00","id":815085,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/810975-power-tiers-in-2e?p=815077#post815077\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How... how does anything we've said suggest that? And why did you quote me, I wasn't even talking to you.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm sorry, perhaps I was confused, I'll relay the conversation from my perspective and see if that makes anymore sense.<br /> <br /> MCN said that the idea that mages can do anything is an exaggeration because mages have limits. As examples he described limits that mages experience within 1st Edition Mage: The Awakening (the only book we have).<br /> <br /> Multiple other uses immediately responded with assertions that those specific limits were being removed. I assumed that these remarks were intended to be relevant to the conversation thus were suggesting that because the 1st edition mage limits were being removed that they wouldn't then be replaced by something else.<br /> <br /> Your comment appeared to be on this same topic, covered the points, was the most recent and was one of the shortest and thus easiest to quote. So I quoted your comment to jump into that conversational thread (since this thread is large enough to now cover multiple issues and responding without anything to identify what I was addressing would be confusing).<br /> <br /> So I'm curious. If you weren't saying what I thought... what were you saying?<br /> <br /> <i><b>Edit:</b> It is entirely probable that I'm just completely confused. This is a massive sprawling thread and I've really started losing track of what people are arguing. I'm sorry if I read something into your post that you didn't mean or if my response was insulting. I got a lot snarkier than I should have.</i>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":6748,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6748-michael-kenner","user":"Michael Kenner","date":". 01-23-2016, 07:05 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6748-michael-kenner","name":"Michael Kenner","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6748_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"380"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-23T16:32:44-08:00","id":815104,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael Kenner</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/810975-power-tiers-in-2e?p=815084#post815084\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm sorry, I think some element of my tone got lost in putting this to text. That's always the risk to being unnecessarily snarky and I should take more care to avoid that.<br /> <br /> I was expressing how strange it was that people seemed to think that he would take all limitations out of Mage because that's what people seemed to be arguing on this thread previously. That absurd idea of a game without any limits isn't what I expect Dave to release, it's what people seemed to be describing, utterly mystifying me.</div> </div> </div> </div>Replacing one strawman with another isn't exactly a rousing endorsement of whatever level of snark you were going for. As I'm sure the helpful combination of the application of common sense and not disingenuously reading the arguments presented would have made that response unnecessary in the first place.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-23T16:37:20-08:00","id":815106,"title":"","content":"This is a thread about 2e power tiers, and I was just pointing out that MCN had made very specific arguments about precisely why mages weren't as powerful as people thought that were based <i>entirely </i>on stuff we knew was gone. He probably had the general gist of a good point, but his argument for it was going in completely the wrong direction because it was based on false premises. <br /> <br /> I don't like seeing a good point sank by a bad argument.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-23T16:42:39-08:00","id":815108,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/810975-power-tiers-in-2e?p=815106#post815106\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is a thread about 2e power tiers, and I was just pointing out that MCN had made very specific arguments about precisely why mages weren't as powerful as people thought that were based <i>entirely </i>on stuff we knew was gone. He probably had the general gist of a good point, but his argument for it was going in completely the wrong direction because it was based on false premises.<br /> <br /> I don't like seeing a good point sank by a bad argument.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh I see. Thanks for clearing that up. Sorry for getting argumentative and rude.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6748-michael-kenner","name":"Michael Kenner","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6748_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"380"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-23T18:21:08-08:00","id":815161,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael Kenner</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/810975-power-tiers-in-2e?p=815049#post815049\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Though if the book does say that Mages now do everything, with no limitations whatsoever and have no challenges (which strangely is what people seem to be arguing here), that book is getting deleted.</div> </div> </div> </div>That is not what we are suggesting at all. Simply that the mechanics for spells allows for the mage to have more options when it comes to &quot;what actions can I take&quot; than something with a number of powerful but specific abilities. Mages are more versatile than vampires.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-24T06:46:13-08:00","id":815410,"title":"","content":"Can anyone give actual links? Because, in my experience, people tend to make assumptions about what is or is not included based on personal bias. I haven't seen any blog that said that there won't be limits on spells, nor any comment. Simply saying &quot;oh, its somewhere&quot; tells me nothing except that's what you believe was said.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-24T06:56:59-08:00","id":815416,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/810975-power-tiers-in-2e?p=815410#post815410\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can anyone give actual links? Because, in my experience, people tend to make assumptions about what is or is not included based on personal bias. I haven't seen any blog that said that there won't be limits on spells, nor any comment. Simply saying &quot;oh, its somewhere&quot; tells me nothing except that's what you believe was said.</div> </div> </div> </div>It wasn't on the blogs (<i><b>Edit:</b> At least I think it wasn't</i>), it was just a comment from Dave on the forums. Took me a little while to find it because it was from a while back.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/748737-time-arcanum-in-2nd-edition?p=760158#post760158\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...158#post760158</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6748-michael-kenner","name":"Michael Kenner","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6748_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"380"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-24T06:59:39-08:00","id":815418,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/107199-crossover-friendly-mage-rules?p=218982#post218982\">You're welcome.</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-24T07:20:16-08:00","id":815427,"title":"","content":"Thanks Michael.<br /> <br /> Okay, so Spell Limit is still a thing, just called Control now. Still limits the number of spells you can have active at once, which is all my argument was really needs to be relevant. Renaming it doesn't change the heart of the argument. If anything, we might be looking at a more restrictive if you can't pull off the Reach. That's a pretty good limit on spells you can have active at once. Its not a hard limit, but its still a limit.<br /> <br /> If anything, I think the new rules support my arguments better than the old. You can easily contain paradox in the lab, then relax. Preparation being a strength. In the field, you've got all these spells up, now you need a new spell, got all this Reach you've got to deal with, and Paradox breathing down your neck. Things can go very wrong, very quickly if you need a high level effect and you've got several spells running. Hells, it doesn't even need to be on you. Sanctum wards, mage armor, bindings on spirits...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-24T10:03:00-08:00","id":815539,"title":"","content":"Spell Control always existed, and was always called that. People are getting confused about the (entirely seperate) Spell <i>Tolerance</i>, which was in 1e and isn't in 2e.<br /> <br /> Also, Spell Control is actually harsher in 2e than it used to be. It's Gnosis instead of Gnosis + 3.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Dave Brookshaw</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","name":"Dave Brookshaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2081"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-24T10:37:02-08:00","id":815567,"title":"","content":"I dunno, I think a steep, theoretically-endless slope is less harsh than a ceiling, even if the ceiling was higher than the slope starts at.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-24T10:42:06-08:00","id":815570,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/810975-power-tiers-in-2e?p=815567#post815567\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I dunno, I think a steep, theoretically-endless slope is less harsh than a ceiling, even if the ceiling was higher than the slope starts at.</div> </div> </div> </div>The problem with the extra Reach requirement is that it can quickly compound. Imagine a Scene with lots of Spellcasting going two ways. One in which extra Reach pushes you to Paradox-risk on every casting and one in which it does not. The extra Reach for exceeding your Spell Control is not the main problem, getting an extra Paradox die for every Paradox risked <i>on top</i> of the extra Paradox dice from using more Reach is.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Politeness is the lubricant of social intercourse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/272-saibot","name":"saibot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar272_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1063"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-24T11:46:24-08:00","id":815596,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/810975-power-tiers-in-2e?p=811194#post811194\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, while Werewolves' ability to affect change <i>is</i> fairly focused on change through destruction, it would be highly inaccurate to say only whatever is currently in front of them. For one thing, in 2e they have just as many powers to help them find and get to the things they want to destroy as they have powers to help them actually destroy, if not more. They're hunters first and warriors second. Also, have you seen the Gift of the Elementals and the Gift of Weather? werewolves have an easier time blowing up cities or other large areas that pretty much any other splat besides maybe mummies. Powerful mages can accomplish similar large-scale destruction, but the resulting Paradox could be catastrophic, whereas a starting werewolf character can easily create natural disasters with little to no risk to herself.</div> </div> </div> </div> 1e Changeling were better then both at that. A Changeling could use cobble thought to pull a functional mushroom cloud from a nuclear explosion out of someones dreams to wipe out a city, or pull out a tornado or a mountain of TNT, a lake of nitroglistern.<br /> <br /> As for 2e I think everyone, even mortals have gotten a bit more powerful, for example the changes to gaining willpower from vice.<br /> <br /> So far for Changelings its hard to tell right now. Kiths have gotten more powerful, but seemings no longer allow you to buff dice pools like Darklings could do to wits rolls or Fairest to Persence, but they do grant you potentially the ability to have more control over they're intergity stat, in this case clarity, then any other splat short of beasts.<br /> <br /> And we don't know enough about the core template, we know that Changeling can get free of any none iron restraints, that oneironacy, the hedge, pledges are still things, but not much more then that and not the full details of how they work.<br /> <br /> One thing is court mantle seems alot more powerful a merit. Example have 5 dots in the Ivory Court gets you -1 penalty to those lying to you, one dot of the goblin vows merit, 9 again on persausion roles, a personal approach, a three dot retainer, the ability to get a single use of either 5 dots of retainers, resources, or allies, your dots added to certain social rolls with fellow members, your dots in defence against the true fae as long as the free hold bulwark is up.<br /> <br /> So how that compares to a vampire or werewolf I don't know.<br /> <br /> I do know in 1e you could make a homeless person into a millionaire or President America and heavily indebted to you via a single well designed pledge.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-24T13:47:39-08:00","id":815665,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dave Brookshaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/810975-power-tiers-in-2e?p=815539#post815539\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Spell Control always existed, and was always called that. People are getting confused about the (entirely seperate) Spell <i>Tolerance</i>, which was in 1e and isn't in 2e.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is one of those changes that makes me really glad. I understood the game balance reasons for it, but it was just a very difficult mechanic to use at the table, especially with crossovers. I also found that while I understood the difference between Spell Control and Spell Tolerance, keeping track of both became very confusing paperwork, especially since I was also tracking how many vulgar spells I'd cast that scene for Paradox. One of my Mage character-sheets is covered all over the back of it with little tally-marks from trying to manage all of that book-keeping. This new system sounds so much easier.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6748-michael-kenner","name":"Michael Kenner","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6748_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"380"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-24T13:53:09-08:00","id":815667,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>milo v3</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/810975-power-tiers-in-2e?p=815161#post815161\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That is not what we are suggesting at all. Simply that the mechanics for spells allows for the mage to have more options when it comes to &quot;what actions can I take&quot; than something with a number of powerful but specific abilities. Mages are more versatile than vampires.</div> </div> </div> </div>I just realized I'd responded to Elfive but hadn't also responded to your post here. I understand what you meant now. I was just a little confused about what people were saying and I let a bad day and grumpiness yesterday turn me rude and argumentative. I'm sorry about that. (This apology also goes out to anyone else in the same category there).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6748-michael-kenner","name":"Michael Kenner","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6748_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"380"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-25T06:37:53-08:00","id":816054,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dave Brookshaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/810975-power-tiers-in-2e?p=815539#post815539\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Spell Control always existed, and was always called that.</div> </div> </div> </div> Huh. Where did I get Limit from then? *Scratches head* I could have sworn it was called Limit.... my mistake on that then. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\">I dunno, I think a steep, theoretically-endless slope is less harsh than a ceiling, even if the ceiling was higher than the slope starts at.</span></div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"> In a sterile white room where the mage has complete control over everything and can prepare his spells for a day? Sure. I completely agree with that. Mages are awesome at preparation. They even get larger dice pools from more and better Yantra in this situation. <br /> <br /> Its in the field that it falls apart. My argument always was that mage versatility was sharply limited when done in the field on the fly. And, yes, I'm pretty sure that mages will worry about Reach and Paradox - its like having a werewolf's fear of falling into Kuruth. Theoretically, you're stronger for it. Realistically, very much bad things happen and you want to generally avoid it at almost all cost. Even if its just avoiding a visit from the Guardians of the Veil telling you to knock it off.<br /> <br /> From what I can see, using Yantra in the field tends to be much more difficult and time consuming in a way that just doesn't matter to a mage in their sanctum, and Reach / Paradox a much larger threat to contain. <br /> <br /> Lets pretend that a theoretical Mastigos is in the field, spying on someone/thing supernatural. Our mastigos is going to want to be disguised somehow. A shielding spell up. A mental shield up in case we're dealing with something with mental abilities or influences. Our mastigos also has low level mind reading up. That's four spells, not counting any protecting a sanctum; and our theoretical mage has Gnosis 3. Anything we need to do - cast a Knowing Time spell to detect if drinking something is safe, use that Mind 4 spell to automatically open Doors - we're going to need to spend some time setting up Yantra to use to offset any penalties, and be very careful with our Paradox. Getting Bedlam could be very bad for our mission - cackling insanity does that - and the spell going wild can have some very bad effects, like summoning the Abyss. All that theoretical versatility suddenly sounds more like a calculated risk at best.<br /> <br /> Even if we could contain all that 'dox through Wisdom? You're willing inflicting pain on yourself. That's something most mages don't shrug off casually. Its painful, and pain is something the overwhelming majority of people avoid.</span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-25T08:04:30-08:00","id":816112,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/810975-power-tiers-in-2e?p=816054#post816054\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Lets pretend that a theoretical Mastigos is in the field, spying on someone/thing supernatural. Our mastigos is going to want to be disguised somehow. A shielding spell up. A mental shield up in case we're dealing with something with mental abilities or influences. Our mastigos also has low level mind reading up. That's four spells, not counting any protecting a sanctum; and our theoretical mage has Gnosis 3. Anything we need to do - cast a Knowing Time spell to detect if drinking something is safe, use that Mind 4 spell to automatically open Doors - we're going to need to spend some time setting up Yantra to use to offset any penalties, and be very careful with our Paradox. Getting Bedlam could be very bad for our mission - cackling insanity does that - and the spell going wild can have some very bad effects, like summoning the Abyss. All that theoretical versatility suddenly sounds more like a calculated risk at best.<br /> <br /> Even if we could contain all that 'dox through Wisdom? You're willing inflicting pain on yourself. That's something most mages don't shrug off casually. Its painful, and pain is something the overwhelming majority of people avoid.[/FONT]</div> </div> </div> </div>At least one of these shielding spells is going to be an Attainment and not count against Spell Control, and any spells protecting the mages sanctum should be long lasting and Relinquished from Spell Control. And if the mage ever needs to cast something else, the mind reading spell is fairly non-critical, so the mage could pretty comfortably end it reflexively, cast what he needed to cast, then recast it on his intended target. Sure, there are things to think about, but a clever mage should be able to manage these things fairly reliably.<br /> <br /> Now I'm not saying this is a non-factor, a good mage will almost certainly have to know how to prioritize and manage his spells, but I don't see it as being <i>that</i> big of an issue. Generally, even in 1e when I played mage I only usually walked around with about 4 spells on at any given time, 2 of those being Mage Sight and Mage Shield. With Sight and Shield now both Attainments I should be able to comfortably cut that down to 2 with no loss in efficiency.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2309-ashenrogue","name":"Ashenrogue","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1388"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-25T08:25:57-08:00","id":816125,"title":"","content":"<br /> The whole argument cames down to the idea that &quot;Mages can do anything.&quot; Clearly, you've just established that's not entirely true in your own argument.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-25T08:28:47-08:00","id":816127,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/810975-power-tiers-in-2e?p=816125#post816125\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The whole argument cames down to the idea that &quot;Mages can do anything.&quot; Clearly, you've just established that's not entirely true in your own argument.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well if you're asking if they <i>can</i> do anything, the answer is yes, with the right number of dots in the right arcana. Now if they <i>should</i> is a completely different question with a completely different answer. I was answering for a mage without the right number of dots in the right arcana.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2309-ashenrogue","name":"Ashenrogue","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1388"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-25T10:20:29-08:00","id":816221,"title":"","content":"Okay, so as a group, Mages can definitely do anything: get enough together working towards the same goal, sky's the limit. But any given individual mage won't be able to do anything, or even most things. Starting Mages get four Arcana at most, generally, and as far as I'm aware, most Mages don't dabble in all the Arcana, they specialize in a few. I'll agree that they get a breadth of power that other supernaturals lack (Arcana being broad themes they can play with, rather than individual powers that do one thing), but they pay for it in Paradox. <br /> <br /> I think there's ways of tiering each splat, but that overall, they tend to balance. Take the strength of individual powers. Mages have the broadest range of powers-per-dot, while Demon has some of the strongest starting abilities. However, both are limited by their ability to get fuel and the fact that reality itself* smacks them when they try to do to much. On the other hand, Changelings have some of the weakest, most limited powers**, but they can do some of them for free, it's really easy for them to get fuel, and reality itself doesn't punish them. (They may go crazy from it, but that's a different problem...)<br /> <br /> There's something to be said for the imbalance in bonuses gotten on creation, though. Vampires get one Attribute, and can pick which one (via picking which Clan they are). Mages get one Attribute, but it's always either Resolve or Composure. Changelings get...a Skill specialty, in Athletics, Brawl, or Stealth. These are just ones I'm familiar with, but in a crossover game, I would call that a meaningful imbalance (and give the Changeling some XP to make up for it.<br /> <br /> *For a given value of reality.<br /> **Exceptions, like Dream 4, exist.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5695-aceofalmonds","name":"AceOfAlmonds","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5695_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"323"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-25T10:41:03-08:00","id":816251,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AceOfAlmonds</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/810975-power-tiers-in-2e?p=816221#post816221\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">...I think there's ways of tiering each splat, but that overall, they tend to balance. Take the strength of individual powers. Mages have the broadest range of powers-per-dot, while Demon has some of the strongest starting abilities. However, both are limited by their ability to get fuel and the fact that reality itself* smacks them when they try to do to much...</div> </div> </div> </div>Mages do not require Mana to cast from their Ruling Arcana, nor to cast rotes, and in 2e so long as they don't overreach themselves (or cast obviously in front of sleepers) they don't risk Paradox. Similarly, Demons' Embeds are free, and measures can be taken to reduce the risk of Compromise. Indeed if I had to name the two splats who could use their powers most freely, it would be Demons and Mages.<br /> <br /> <b>Edit: </b>It's gonna be really difficult to develop a power tiering system that doesn't have these two splats way at the top. Power, personal and social, is central to both of their themes. They have plenty of limits, but those are primarily narrative and won't be easily reflected in a tier list.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <b>Mod Voice is <u><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">RED</span></u>*</b><br /> <i>*All other colors should be read aloud in the voice of Don Knotts</i><b>.</b> <hr /><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/18519-pendragon-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">Hacks and House Rules Hub Thread</a></b><br /> <br /> <b>CofD Hacks By Splat: <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/13vBLaS5Ua1Ez-cVyK6uFa4ssvYeIIZpoA5GQTXytfcA/edit\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Vampire</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1sqltG7X-C_MdEe00PtVOZmki8V_K1M1FpQtLwTvb2jg/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#006400\">Werewolf</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1bpr1EjQ4RfZ5dz-tXmJJ93P2f_l7fUIUwpPLWs9Z-SI/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800080\">Mage</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1vKpSTktCUuUaqxXncG4txQPtvPclzXlFZEEX7tbrTSg/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Mummy</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Spynbcs_VgCDHdooKWXobZNe6C9CMjONeRTlvXIq9fI/edit?usp=drive_web\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Demon</span></a></b>","edited":{"userid":148,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/148-pendragon","user":"PenDragon","date":". 01-25-2016, 01:51 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/148-pendragon","name":"PenDragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar148_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1657"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-25T10:46:50-08:00","id":816257,"title":"","content":"Also in demonic form demons are literally incapable of running out of aether. If they hit zero they immediately get <i>at least </i>one back, possibly more depending on how the primum roll goes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-25T10:47:38-08:00","id":816260,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PenDragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/810975-power-tiers-in-2e?p=816251#post816251\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mages do not require Mana to cast from their Ruling Arcana, nor to cast rotes, and in 2e so long as they don't overreach themselves (or cast obviously in front of sleepers) they don't risk Paradox. Similarly, Demons' Embeds are free, and measures can be taken to reduce the risk of Compromise. Indeed if I had to name the two splats who could use their powers most freely, it would be Demons and Mages.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm playing a Mage/Demon crossover, so we're having lots of fun with this. Though mainly it's mostly the mages and other two demons screwing with my character, who's cover is a cop.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9830-reshyshira","name":"ReshyShira","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9830_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"589"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-25T11:01:28-08:00","id":816269,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PenDragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/810975-power-tiers-in-2e?p=816251#post816251\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Edit: </b>It's gonna be really difficult to develop a power tiering system that doesn't have these two splats way at the top. Power, personal and social, is central to both of their themes. They have plenty of limits, but those are primarily narrative and won't be easily reflected in a tier list.</div> </div> </div> </div>Distasteful as you may find it, if it's that hard to develop a tier system where Mages and Demons don't get at the top of list, it's a pretty good sign that those two splat are flat out better than everything else in potential.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2547-elderand","name":"Elderand","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"98"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-25T11:08:09-08:00","id":816274,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elderand</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/810975-power-tiers-in-2e?p=816269#post816269\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Distasteful as you may find it, if it's that hard to develop a tier system where Mages and Demons don't get at the top of list, it's a pretty good sign that those two splat are flat out better than everything else in potential.</div> </div> </div> </div>I won't argue against that, in fact I'll agree. My argument has never been that you can't assemble a tier list, it's that you can't assemble a <i>practical </i>tier list. To use some Mage terminology the <i>platonic ideal</i> Mage or Demon character has almost limitless potential. However, when filtered through the Abyssal layers of Storyteller, Narrative, Character and Player the final result tends to fall short of the ideal vision.<br /> <br /> <b>Edit: </b>But, as other's have pointed out, this thread <b>is </b>about making a tier list. I simply chimed in to clear up the misconception about power access, and weigh in on the probable placement of both splats. I'll admit, I came off as a tad of a Negative Nancy. Sorry about that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <b>Mod Voice is <u><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">RED</span></u>*</b><br /> <i>*All other colors should be read aloud in the voice of Don Knotts</i><b>.</b> <hr /><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/18519-pendragon-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">Hacks and House Rules Hub Thread</a></b><br /> <br /> <b>CofD Hacks By Splat: <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/13vBLaS5Ua1Ez-cVyK6uFa4ssvYeIIZpoA5GQTXytfcA/edit\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Vampire</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1sqltG7X-C_MdEe00PtVOZmki8V_K1M1FpQtLwTvb2jg/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#006400\">Werewolf</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1bpr1EjQ4RfZ5dz-tXmJJ93P2f_l7fUIUwpPLWs9Z-SI/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800080\">Mage</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1vKpSTktCUuUaqxXncG4txQPtvPclzXlFZEEX7tbrTSg/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Mummy</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Spynbcs_VgCDHdooKWXobZNe6C9CMjONeRTlvXIq9fI/edit?usp=drive_web\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Demon</span></a></b>","edited":{"userid":148,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/148-pendragon","user":"PenDragon","date":". 01-25-2016, 02:17 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/148-pendragon","name":"PenDragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar148_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1657"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-25T11:19:11-08:00","id":816283,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PenDragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/810975-power-tiers-in-2e?p=816251#post816251\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mages do not require Mana to cast from their Ruling Arcana, nor to cast rotes, and in 2e so long as they don't overreach themselves (or cast obviously in front of sleepers) they don't risk Paradox. Similarly, Demons' Embeds are free, and measures can be taken to reduce the risk of Compromise. Indeed if I had to name the two splats who could use their powers most freely, it would be Demons and Mages.<br /> <br /> <b>Edit: </b>It's gonna be really difficult to develop a power tiering system that doesn't have these two splats way at the top. Power, personal and social, is central to both of their themes. They have plenty of limits, but those are primarily narrative and won't be easily reflected in a tier list.</div> </div> </div> </div>I thought that, Ruling Arcana or no, if you're reaching, you're spending Mana. But I may be incorrect about that too, and there are a number of things you can do without Mana. I did forget Embeds are free, but saying there's steps you can take to mitigate the drawback doesn't negate it. You can negate any given drawback. Compromise is, IMO, one of the worse drawbacks of the splats; I'd put it near Paradox, and just below Death Rage.<br /> <br /> I'd argue Mage and Demon are near the bottom of the &quot;how easy is it to refuel&quot; list.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5695-aceofalmonds","name":"AceOfAlmonds","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5695_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"323"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-25T11:27:28-08:00","id":816288,"title":"","content":"I repeat. <i>Literally incapable of running out of aether.</i>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-25T11:36:01-08:00","id":816293,"title":"","content":"Yay but thats when they are in demonic form. They git to roll their power stat to get back aether and get back at least 1. But if they use that too often the God Machine will find them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10820-blakemikizuki","name":"Blakemikizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10820_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"280"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-25T11:36:07-08:00","id":816294,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AceOfAlmonds</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/810975-power-tiers-in-2e?p=816283#post816283\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I thought that, Ruling Arcana or no, if you're reaching, you're spending Mana. But I may be incorrect about that too, and there are a number of things you can do without Mana. I did forget Embeds are free, but saying there's steps you can take to mitigate the drawback doesn't negate it. You can negate any given drawback. Compromise is, IMO, one of the worse drawbacks of the splats; I'd put it near Paradox, and just below Death Rage.</div> </div> </div> </div>According to DaveB's spoilers Mana is spent to: Activate certain Attainments (like the active version of Mage Sight), cast from Non-ruling Arcana, and mitigate Paradox. A Mage can cast freely, and Reach freely from their Ruling Arcana.<br /> <br /> Compromise is unpleasant, I'll give you that. Though I'd put it well above Death Rage, because Compromise it considerably more manageable and a tier list should take into account the splats ability to work around their limits. Paradox...we'll have to see how it turns out in 2e. In terms of raw power Paradox can actually make a spell stronger, and is among the most player manageable drawbacks. Indeed, if the Mage doesn't care about occasionally fucking reality it can be employed to his benefit when times get tough.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I'd argue Mage and Demon are near the bottom of the &quot;how easy is it to refuel&quot; list. </div> </div> </div>Where they stand depends a lot on where they put their merit dots. A Mage who invested in a hollow, has a bunch of Prime, or the sort of Status and influence they need to easily acquire Tass will have a fairly easy time with Mana. And any Mage with a Legacy can perform oblations outside of a hollow for mana. Demons...I'll agree with you there. It is quite deliberately a risk for Demons to refuel their Aether, but they still have astonishing power in their Embeds.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <b>Mod Voice is <u><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">RED</span></u>*</b><br /> <i>*All other colors should be read aloud in the voice of Don Knotts</i><b>.</b> <hr /><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/18519-pendragon-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">Hacks and House Rules Hub Thread</a></b><br /> <br /> <b>CofD Hacks By Splat: <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/13vBLaS5Ua1Ez-cVyK6uFa4ssvYeIIZpoA5GQTXytfcA/edit\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Vampire</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1sqltG7X-C_MdEe00PtVOZmki8V_K1M1FpQtLwTvb2jg/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#006400\">Werewolf</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1bpr1EjQ4RfZ5dz-tXmJJ93P2f_l7fUIUwpPLWs9Z-SI/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800080\">Mage</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1vKpSTktCUuUaqxXncG4txQPtvPclzXlFZEEX7tbrTSg/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Mummy</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Spynbcs_VgCDHdooKWXobZNe6C9CMjONeRTlvXIq9fI/edit?usp=drive_web\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Demon</span></a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/148-pendragon","name":"PenDragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar148_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1657"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-25T11:39:52-08:00","id":816301,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/810975-power-tiers-in-2e?p=816288#post816288\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I repeat. <i>Literally incapable of running out of aether.</i></div> </div> </div> </div>While in Demon form, they can roll to get some back, but they can't continue to roll that again and again. While in Cover, no, not at all. Demon form has its own very major drawbacks, which is why most Demons don't run around un-Covered because of the Aether boost.<br /> <br /> New flippant Tier system: How much does reality want to punch you in the face?<br /> <br /> Lots: Promethean (literally poison the world)<br /> Some: Demon, Mage (between the G-M and Paradox)<br /> A bit: Vampire (mostly the sun hates you)<br /> Not really: Changeling, Werewolf, Hunter (only enough to give you PTSD, but really, everyone gets that)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5695,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5695-aceofalmonds","user":"AceOfAlmonds","date":". 01-25-2016, 02:42 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5695-aceofalmonds","name":"AceOfAlmonds","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5695_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"323"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-25T11:46:01-08:00","id":816306,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AceOfAlmonds</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/810975-power-tiers-in-2e?p=816301#post816301\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> While in Demon form, they can roll to get some back, but they can't continue to roll that again and again. While in Cover, no, not at all. Demon form has its own very major drawbacks, which is why most Demons don't run around un-Covered because of the Aether boost.<br /> <br /> New flippant Tier system: How much does reality want to punch you in the face?<br /> <br /> Lots: Promethean (literally poison the world)<br /> Some: Demon, Mage (between the G-M and Paradox)<br /> A bit: Vampire (mostly the sun hates you)<br /> Not really: Changeling, Werewolf, Hunter (only enough to give you PTSD, but really, everyone gets that)</div> </div> </div> </div>I dunno, Changelings as per the 2e spoilers are constantly hunted by living stories that seek to torment and imprison them. And Werewolves are largely loathed by spirits, the totemic embodiments of worldly concepts. Oh, and Mummies who aren't fulfilling their purpose are constantly falling apart.<br /> <br /> Sin-Eaters are fine. Though I see that as one of the lines greatest faults.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <b>Mod Voice is <u><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">RED</span></u>*</b><br /> <i>*All other colors should be read aloud in the voice of Don Knotts</i><b>.</b> <hr /><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/18519-pendragon-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">Hacks and House Rules Hub Thread</a></b><br /> <br /> <b>CofD Hacks By Splat: <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/13vBLaS5Ua1Ez-cVyK6uFa4ssvYeIIZpoA5GQTXytfcA/edit\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Vampire</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1sqltG7X-C_MdEe00PtVOZmki8V_K1M1FpQtLwTvb2jg/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#006400\">Werewolf</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1bpr1EjQ4RfZ5dz-tXmJJ93P2f_l7fUIUwpPLWs9Z-SI/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800080\">Mage</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1vKpSTktCUuUaqxXncG4txQPtvPclzXlFZEEX7tbrTSg/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Mummy</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Spynbcs_VgCDHdooKWXobZNe6C9CMjONeRTlvXIq9fI/edit?usp=drive_web\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Demon</span></a></b>","edited":{"userid":148,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/148-pendragon","user":"PenDragon","date":". 01-25-2016, 02:49 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/148-pendragon","name":"PenDragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar148_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1657"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-25T12:08:46-08:00","id":816326,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PenDragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/810975-power-tiers-in-2e?p=816294#post816294\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">According to DaveB's spoilers Mana is spent to: Activate certain Attainments (like the active version of Mage Sight), cast from Non-ruling Arcana, and mitigate Paradox. A Mage can cast freely, and Reach freely from their Ruling Arcana.<br /> <br /> Compromise is unpleasant, I'll give you that. Though I'd put it well above Death Rage, because Compromise it considerably more manageable and a tier list should take into account the splats ability to work around their limits. Paradox...we'll have to see how it turns out in 2e. In terms of raw power Paradox can actually make a spell stronger, and is among the most player manageable drawbacks. Indeed, if the Mage doesn't care about occasionally fucking reality it can be employed to his benefit when times get tough.<br /> <br /> <br /> Where they stand depends a lot on where they put their merit dots. A Mage who invested in a hollow, has a bunch of Prime, or the sort of Status and influence they need to easily acquire Tass will have a fairly easy time with Mana. And any Mage with a Legacy can perform oblations outside of a hollow for mana. Demons...I'll agree with you there. It is quite deliberately a risk for Demons to refuel their Aether, but they still have astonishing power in their Embeds.</div> </div> </div> </div>Gotcha. I was working from my knowledge of 1e, hence my confusion/assumptions on Mana expendature.<br /> <br /> Death Rage/Frenzy would be what I consider the worse/harshest drawbacks, as they completely cede player control to the ST, and make everything afterword harder. Paradox is a crapshoot on how it turns out, and has a sliding scale; Compromise is always bad and adds complications, but the worst end of Paradox is (as of 1e) worse than Compromise. Again, in my opinion <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Getting Mana for Merits is an option, but it's still something you have to deliberately mitigate, and when you're spending Merits on that, you're lacking them elsewhere. Legacies are an option, but only later in the game. Compare to what I'd call the easy-refuel splats: Prometheans get fuel daily (though it's small); Vampires and Changelings just need to find a human (or something close enough). Changelings don't even risk problems when getting their fuel (unlike Vamps). And all of them can get fuel even easier via merit dots.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PenDragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/810975-power-tiers-in-2e?p=816306#post816306\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I dunno, Changelings as per the 2e spoilers are constantly hunted by living stories that seek to torment and imprison them. And Werewolves are largely loathed by spirits, the totemic embodiments of worldly concepts. Oh, and Mummies who aren't fulfilling their purpose are constantly falling apart.<br /> <br /> Sin-Eaters are fine. Though I see that as one of the lines greatest faults.</div> </div> </div> </div>I was excluding Huntsmen, since 2e isn't out yet and those are more of a &quot;bad guy targeted at your splat&quot;, which every single line has (although playing the ranking game with &quot;stuff what wants to end you&quot; might also be a fun flippant tier). Spirit-hatred might put Werewolves a tier up, that's fair. I did not know that about Mummies; I might put that between &quot;Some&quot; and &quot;A bit&quot;, since that's harsh, but mitigatable short of forgoing using your powers.<br /> <br /> Sin-Eaters can go at the very bottom. They do win &quot;most difficult to refuel&quot;, though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5695-aceofalmonds","name":"AceOfAlmonds","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5695_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"323"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-25T12:33:33-08:00","id":816343,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AceOfAlmonds</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/810975-power-tiers-in-2e?p=816326#post816326\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Getting Mana for Merits is an option, but it's still something you have to deliberately mitigate, and when you're spending Merits on that, you're lacking them elsewhere. Legacies are an option, but only later in the game. Compare to what I'd call the easy-refuel splats: Prometheans get fuel daily (though it's small); Vampires and Changelings just need to find a human (or something close enough). Changelings don't even risk problems when getting their fuel (unlike Vamps). And all of them can get fuel even easier via merit dots.<br /> ...<br /> Sin-Eaters can go at the very bottom. They do win &quot;most difficult to refuel&quot;, though.</div> </div> </div> </div>Legacies are another 2e change, you can join a Legacy at Gnosis 2, which makes them far more accessible. Though you are correct that Vampires and Changelings (at least 1e Changelings) have easiest access to their fuel, they also have to do harm to gain it.<br /> <br /> If I had to Tier fuel access it would be something like:<br /> \u2022 <b>Tier 1: Changelings</b> - They can suck it right out of people who are feeling a certain emotion, and probably won't be caught in the act.<br /> \u2022 <b>Tier 2: Vampires/Prometheans</b> - Both can recharge quickly, but must be careful about doing it in public. (I'm hoping 2e makes it harder on Prommies).<br /> \u2022 <b>Tier 3: Mages/Beasts</b> - Both can gain their fuel fairly easily, but require some setup to achieve it. Beasts risk more, but still have easy access to their opportunities. Mages without a Legacy fall one tier.<br /> \u2022 <b>Tier 4: Werewolves/Sin-Eaters</b> - Both are stuck relying on rare and specific locations, agreements, or long drawn out procedures (hunting). Werewolves willing to eat people jump up to Tier 2.<br /> \u2022 <b>Tier 5: Mummies/Demons</b> - It's fucking hard to get Pillars back, and while your sitting in your Tomb recharging your Sekhem is still falling. And Demons have to sidle silently up to their greatest adversary to soak up Aether, which is not an easy option.<br /> <br /> This list is, however, very dependent on character and setting. A vampire or changeling who is unwilling to harm others will have a much harder time, while a Mage or Werewolf who is sparing with their fuel usage (as both can reasonably be) may find that they simply never want for fuel.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <b>Mod Voice is <u><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">RED</span></u>*</b><br /> <i>*All other colors should be read aloud in the voice of Don Knotts</i><b>.</b> <hr /><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/18519-pendragon-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">Hacks and House Rules Hub Thread</a></b><br /> <br /> <b>CofD Hacks By Splat: <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/13vBLaS5Ua1Ez-cVyK6uFa4ssvYeIIZpoA5GQTXytfcA/edit\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Vampire</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1sqltG7X-C_MdEe00PtVOZmki8V_K1M1FpQtLwTvb2jg/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#006400\">Werewolf</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1bpr1EjQ4RfZ5dz-tXmJJ93P2f_l7fUIUwpPLWs9Z-SI/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800080\">Mage</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1vKpSTktCUuUaqxXncG4txQPtvPclzXlFZEEX7tbrTSg/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Mummy</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Spynbcs_VgCDHdooKWXobZNe6C9CMjONeRTlvXIq9fI/edit?usp=drive_web\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Demon</span></a></b>","edited":{"userid":148,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/148-pendragon","user":"PenDragon","date":". 01-25-2016, 03:35 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/148-pendragon","name":"PenDragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar148_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1657"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-25T12:48:57-08:00","id":816364,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PenDragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/810975-power-tiers-in-2e?p=816343#post816343\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Legacies are another 2e change, you can join a Legacy at Gnosis 2, which makes them far more accessible. Though you are correct that Vampires and Changelings (at least 1e Changelings) have easiest access to their fuel, they also have to do harm to gain it.<br /> <br /> If I had to Tier fuel access it would be something like:<br /> \u2022 <b>Tier 1: Changelings</b> - They can suck it right out of people who are feeling a certain emotion, and probably won't be caught in the act.<br /> \u2022 <b>Tier 2: Vampires/Prometheans</b> - Both can recharge quickly, but must be careful about doing it in public. (I'm hoping 2e makes it harder on Prommies).<br /> \u2022 <b>Tier 3: Mages/Beasts</b> - Both can gain their fuel fairly easily, but require some setup to achieve it. Beasts risk more, but still have easy access to their opportunities. Mages without a Legacy fall one tier.<br /> \u2022 <b>Tier 4: Werewolves/Sin-Eaters</b> - Both are stuck relying on rare and specific locations, agreements, or long drawn out procedures (hunting). Werewolves willing to eat people jump up to Tier 2.<br /> \u2022 <b>Tier 5: Mummies/Demons</b> - It's fucking hard to get Pillars back, and while your sitting in your Tomb recharging your Sekhem is still falling. And Demons have to sidle silently up to their greatest adversary to soak up Aether, which is not an easy option.<br /> <br /> This list is, however, very dependent on character and setting. A vampire or changeling who is unwilling to harm others will have a much harder time, while a Mage or Werewolf who is sparing with their fuel usage (as both can reasonably be) may find that they simply never want for fuel.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree with almost all of this. With Changelings, though, gathering Glamour does no inherent harm to those it's gathered from, as far as I'm aware. There are harm-causing methods of getting humans emotional enough, but it's not an inherent unavoidable thing (as opposed to, say, Vampires).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5695-aceofalmonds","name":"AceOfAlmonds","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5695_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"323"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-25T12:50:58-08:00","id":816367,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AceOfAlmonds</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/810975-power-tiers-in-2e?p=816364#post816364\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I agree with almost all of this. With Changelings, though, gathering Glamour does no inherent harm to those it's gathered from, as far as I'm aware. There are harm-causing methods of getting humans emotional enough, but it's not an inherent unavoidable thing (as opposed to, say, Vampires).</div> </div> </div> </div>I believe harvesting Glamour is supposed to slowly sap the feeling from a person, over time dulling their joys, fears and experiences until everything is just...grey. However, 1e doesn't really do a great job of conveying that. That or I'm totally misremembering.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <b>Mod Voice is <u><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">RED</span></u>*</b><br /> <i>*All other colors should be read aloud in the voice of Don Knotts</i><b>.</b> <hr /><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/18519-pendragon-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">Hacks and House Rules Hub Thread</a></b><br /> <br /> <b>CofD Hacks By Splat: <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/13vBLaS5Ua1Ez-cVyK6uFa4ssvYeIIZpoA5GQTXytfcA/edit\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Vampire</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1sqltG7X-C_MdEe00PtVOZmki8V_K1M1FpQtLwTvb2jg/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#006400\">Werewolf</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1bpr1EjQ4RfZ5dz-tXmJJ93P2f_l7fUIUwpPLWs9Z-SI/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800080\">Mage</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1vKpSTktCUuUaqxXncG4txQPtvPclzXlFZEEX7tbrTSg/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Mummy</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Spynbcs_VgCDHdooKWXobZNe6C9CMjONeRTlvXIq9fI/edit?usp=drive_web\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Demon</span></a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/148-pendragon","name":"PenDragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar148_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1657"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-25T13:13:23-08:00","id":816378,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PenDragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/810975-power-tiers-in-2e?p=816367#post816367\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I believe harvesting Glamour is supposed to slowly sap the feeling from a person, over time dulling their joys, fears and experiences until everything is just...grey. However, 1e doesn't really do a great job of conveying that. That or I'm totally misremembering.</div> </div> </div> </div>It might be out of one of the splats? Or one paragraph of fluff in the core, but without mechanics, or a sidebar option. It sounds a little familiar, but as the sort of thing that <i>may </i>cause harm over time if a Changeling constantly hits the same person up for Glamour, not something inherent, constant, and hard to avoid. That, and there's always the other Glamour-option of Hedgefruit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5695-aceofalmonds","name":"AceOfAlmonds","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5695_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"323"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-25T13:18:01-08:00","id":816380,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AceOfAlmonds</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/810975-power-tiers-in-2e?p=816378#post816378\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It might be out of one of the splats? Or one paragraph of fluff in the core, but without mechanics, or a sidebar option. It sounds a little familiar, but as the sort of thing that <i>may </i>cause harm over time if a Changeling constantly hits the same person up for Glamour, not something inherent, constant, and hard to avoid. That, and there's always the other Glamour-option of Hedgefruit.</div> </div> </div> </div>Right, regardless it's really easy to do. The Changelings in my mixed games have never wanted for Glamour, and the system doesn't punish them for harvesting it. I don't really see it as a problem, though I do hope 2e delves more into the drawbacks. Being an emotional vampire really should do some harm, this is a horror setting after all.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <b>Mod Voice is <u><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">RED</span></u>*</b><br /> <i>*All other colors should be read aloud in the voice of Don Knotts</i><b>.</b> <hr /><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/18519-pendragon-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">Hacks and House Rules Hub Thread</a></b><br /> <br /> <b>CofD Hacks By Splat: <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/13vBLaS5Ua1Ez-cVyK6uFa4ssvYeIIZpoA5GQTXytfcA/edit\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Vampire</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1sqltG7X-C_MdEe00PtVOZmki8V_K1M1FpQtLwTvb2jg/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#006400\">Werewolf</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1bpr1EjQ4RfZ5dz-tXmJJ93P2f_l7fUIUwpPLWs9Z-SI/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800080\">Mage</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1vKpSTktCUuUaqxXncG4txQPtvPclzXlFZEEX7tbrTSg/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Mummy</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Spynbcs_VgCDHdooKWXobZNe6C9CMjONeRTlvXIq9fI/edit?usp=drive_web\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Demon</span></a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/148-pendragon","name":"PenDragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar148_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1657"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-25T13:19:57-08:00","id":816382,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PenDragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/810975-power-tiers-in-2e?p=816367#post816367\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I believe harvesting Glamour is supposed to slowly sap the feeling from a person, over time dulling their joys, fears and experiences until everything is just...grey. However, 1e doesn't really do a great job of conveying that. That or I'm totally misremembering.</div> </div> </div> </div>Close, but not quite.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Harvesting Glamour in this fashion doesn\u2019t actually drain energy; the mortal does not suddenly feel less emotional as the changeling harvests the mortal\u2019s feelings. Many changelings take comfort in this fact, interpreting the lack of visible harm as less of a violation. However, whispers tell of mortals who are subjected to regular harvesting over a long period of time eventually losing some indescribable, yet vital spark. While these ravaged souls remain the stuff of rumors, it is enough of a fear that many changelings avoid tapping the same resource too often, especially in the case of friends or loved ones. Just in case. </div> </div> </div>There is also no consequences (apparently) from obtaining Glamour via Dreamwalking, Pledges or Hedge Bounties (beyond the obvious perils of such actions).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/872434-shadow-knight-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10056-shadowknight1224","name":"ShadowKnight1224","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"975"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-25T13:25:49-08:00","id":816387,"title":"","content":"That's what I was recalling. Thanks for clarifying.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <b>Mod Voice is <u><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">RED</span></u>*</b><br /> <i>*All other colors should be read aloud in the voice of Don Knotts</i><b>.</b> <hr /><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/18519-pendragon-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">Hacks and House Rules Hub Thread</a></b><br /> <br /> <b>CofD Hacks By Splat: <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/13vBLaS5Ua1Ez-cVyK6uFa4ssvYeIIZpoA5GQTXytfcA/edit\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Vampire</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1sqltG7X-C_MdEe00PtVOZmki8V_K1M1FpQtLwTvb2jg/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#006400\">Werewolf</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1bpr1EjQ4RfZ5dz-tXmJJ93P2f_l7fUIUwpPLWs9Z-SI/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800080\">Mage</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1vKpSTktCUuUaqxXncG4txQPtvPclzXlFZEEX7tbrTSg/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Mummy</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Spynbcs_VgCDHdooKWXobZNe6C9CMjONeRTlvXIq9fI/edit?usp=drive_web\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Demon</span></a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/148-pendragon","name":"PenDragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar148_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1657"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-25T13:32:14-08:00","id":816392,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PenDragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/810975-power-tiers-in-2e?p=816343#post816343\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Legacies are another 2e change, you can join a Legacy at Gnosis 2, which makes them far more accessible. Though you are correct that Vampires and Changelings (at least 1e Changelings) have easiest access to their fuel, they also have to do harm to gain it.<br /> <br /> If I had to Tier fuel access it would be something like:<br /> \u2022 <b>Tier 1: Changelings</b> - They can suck it right out of people who are feeling a certain emotion, and probably won't be caught in the act.<br /> \u2022 <b>Tier 2: Vampires/Prometheans</b> - Both can recharge quickly, but must be careful about doing it in public. (I'm hoping 2e makes it harder on Prommies).<br /> \u2022 <b>Tier 3: Mages/Beasts</b> - Both can gain their fuel fairly easily, but require some setup to achieve it. Beasts risk more, but still have easy access to their opportunities. Mages without a Legacy fall one tier.<br /> \u2022 <b>Tier 4: Werewolves/Sin-Eaters</b> - Both are stuck relying on rare and specific locations, agreements, or long drawn out procedures (hunting). Werewolves willing to eat people jump up to Tier 2.<br /> \u2022 <b>Tier 5: Mummies/Demons</b> - It's fucking hard to get Pillars back, and while your sitting in your Tomb recharging your Sekhem is still falling. And Demons have to sidle silently up to their greatest adversary to soak up Aether, which is not an easy option.<br /> <br /> This list is, however, very dependent on character and setting. A vampire or changeling who is unwilling to harm others will have a much harder time, while a Mage or Werewolf who is sparing with their fuel usage (as both can reasonably be) may find that they simply never want for fuel.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> With respect to mages, a mid-level proficiency in Prime, such as would be possessed by virtually all Obrimos, makes Mama acquisition quite easy and would probably warrant an effective bump-up to Tier 2.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","name":"branford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar618_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1904"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-25T13:40:37-08:00","id":816401,"title":"","content":"Are we taking pattern scouring into account with this?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-25T13:47:50-08:00","id":816407,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PenDragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/810975-power-tiers-in-2e?p=816380#post816380\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Right, regardless it's really easy to do. The Changelings in my mixed games have never wanted for Glamour, and the system doesn't punish them for harvesting it. I don't really see it as a problem, though I do hope 2e delves more into the drawbacks. Being an emotional vampire really should do some harm, this is a horror setting after all.</div> </div> </div> </div>Why? Changelings have the most restrictive magical abilities. Plus, causing lasting damage is Beasts shtick.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9830-reshyshira","name":"ReshyShira","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9830_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"589"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-25T13:51:51-08:00","id":816409,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/810975-power-tiers-in-2e?p=816401#post816401\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Are we taking pattern scouring into account with this?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Why wouldn't we if ratings simply reflect &quot;easiest access to fuel&quot; without other set limitations?<br /> <br /> Mages as a whole truly have a lot of options for virtually everything. <br /> <br /> I also believe pattern scouring is getting an update in 2e and will be further modified by the yet unknown Life 2 Arcana Attainment.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","name":"branford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar618_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1904"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-25T13:55:06-08:00","id":816413,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>branford</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/810975-power-tiers-in-2e?p=816392#post816392\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> With respect to mages, a mid-level proficiency in Prime, such as would be possessed by virtually all Obrimos, makes Mama acquisition quite easy and would probably warrant an effective bump-up to Tier 2.</div> </div> </div> </div>So 1/5 of Mages get to be on Tier 2, that seems fair. Most sit at 3, even with pattern scouring (because while that's always available, it's not safe, and it's not really a good idea. A better idea than eating people, but still not a good idea.) /opinion","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5695-aceofalmonds","name":"AceOfAlmonds","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5695_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"323"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-25T23:59:42-08:00","id":816712,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Sin-Eaters are fine. Though I see that as one of the lines greatest faults. </div> </div> </div>Weirdly that's one of the reasons I love sin-eater.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-26T01:21:52-08:00","id":816737,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AceOfAlmonds</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/810975-power-tiers-in-2e?p=816413#post816413\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So 1/5 of Mages get to be on Tier 2, that seems fair. Most sit at 3, even with pattern scouring (because while that's always available, it's not safe, and it's not really a good idea. A better idea than eating people, but still not a good idea.) /opinion</div> </div> </div> </div>While you have to spend a point from an attribute or a HL on pattern scouring, Mages also get an extra point in an attribute. So if you spend just that extra attribute point on pattern scouring that gives you 3 mana per day without any drawback compared to a most other splats.<br /> You can also sacrifice one small animal per day for an extra point of mana, giving you a base regeneration of 4 mana/day.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/158192-what-s-your-custom-legacy?p=1109906#post1109906\" target=\"_blank\">My custom legacy</a> (2e)- The Disciples of Rathma - Life/Death focused Moros/Thyrsus Legacy, comments appreciated","edited":{"userid":166,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/166-joker","user":"Joker","date":". 01-26-2016, 04:24 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/166-joker","name":"Joker","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"477"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-26T01:32:16-08:00","id":816741,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Joker</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/810975-power-tiers-in-2e?p=816737#post816737\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> While you have to spend a point from an attribute or a HL on pattern scouring, Mages also get an extra point in an attribute. So if you spend just that extra attribute point on pattern scouring that gives you 3 mana per day without any drawback compared to a most other splats.</div> </div> </div> </div>Unless I've missed something entirely, neither of the options for the free Attribute dot are in the category that's viable for pattern scouring.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-26T01:39:56-08:00","id":816744,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/810975-power-tiers-in-2e?p=816741#post816741\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Unless I've missed something entirely, neither of the options for the free Attribute dot are in the category that's viable for pattern scouring.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, right. Overlooked the pysical part when rereading the section just now.<br /> So, one from sacrificing a small animal.<br /> (But honestly, sacrificing a single dot from an unimportant attribute every day isn't something I'd consider all that dangerous)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/158192-what-s-your-custom-legacy?p=1109906#post1109906\" target=\"_blank\">My custom legacy</a> (2e)- The Disciples of Rathma - Life/Death focused Moros/Thyrsus Legacy, comments appreciated","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/166-joker","name":"Joker","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"477"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-26T02:24:41-08:00","id":816755,"title":"","content":"I was about to post something similar, but then I realised that as long as you don't make physical tertiary you can distribute the dots in such a way as to make the scoured spread look like a natural staring set.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-26T05:15:30-08:00","id":816792,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PenDragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/810975-power-tiers-in-2e?p=816251#post816251\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Edit: </b>It's gonna be really difficult to develop a power tiering system that doesn't have these two splats way at the top. Power, personal and social, is central to both of their themes. They have plenty of limits, but those are primarily narrative and won't be easily reflected in a tier list.</div> </div> </div> </div> &quot;Power&quot; as a theme doesn't really affect the overall power of the splats. If you want to call them high tier, its because mages, demons, and mummies effectively tier 3 games, when most of the others operate on a smaller scale than that. These games are designed to deal with issues on a global and cosmic scale. <br /> <br /> Also, I don't think that Power is a theme for DtD. I don't see it listed as part of the inspirational material, nor formally anywhere in the introduction. I don't know where you're getting that from.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PenDragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/810975-power-tiers-in-2e?p=816367#post816367\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I believe harvesting Glamour is supposed to slowly sap the feeling from a person, over time dulling their joys, fears and experiences until everything is just...grey. However, 1e doesn't really do a great job of conveying that. That or I'm totally misremembering.</div> </div> </div> </div> That's an optional rule in Rites of Spring, not the default. You also seem to be hyper focused on emotions, not considering that you can get glamour from dreams (which is kinda the same as emotions), fulfilled pledges, and goblin fruits. That's at least two ways of glamour feeding that's not going to hurt anyone. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-26T05:55:07-08:00","id":816811,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/810975-power-tiers-in-2e?p=816755#post816755\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I was about to post something similar, but then I realised that as long as you don't make physical tertiary you can distribute the dots in such a way as to make the scoured spread look like a natural staring set.</div> </div> </div> </div>Honestly, while Mages aren't that great at basic Mana generation without any investment, they get some of the most powerful ways to regenerate their fuelstat of any splat.<br /> Between Hallows, Artifacts (which give mindboggling amounts of mana/day), Prime Arcanum, Legacies, Life Magic to reinforce scoured attributes, mundane Quick Healer Merit so you can easily afford scouring a HL/day, animal/human sacrifice, Familiars, Imbued items with Prime manareg spells, and probably some more I am forgetting. Mages are really spoiled for choice when it comes to getting back Mana.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/158192-what-s-your-custom-legacy?p=1109906#post1109906\" target=\"_blank\">My custom legacy</a> (2e)- The Disciples of Rathma - Life/Death focused Moros/Thyrsus Legacy, comments appreciated","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/166-joker","name":"Joker","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"477"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-26T16:20:12-08:00","id":817230,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dave Brookshaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/810975-power-tiers-in-2e?p=815539#post815539\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Spell Control always existed, and was always called that. People are getting confused about the (entirely seperate) Spell <i>Tolerance</i>, which was in 1e and isn't in 2e.</div> </div> </div> </div>That may at least partially be because 1e Spell Tolerance was the one where you could go past the limit at the cost of bad stuff happening (penalties to all actions as your Pattern is overloaded with spells, IIRC), whereas Spell Control was an absolute hard cap you could never exceed. 2e Spell Control lets you get past it, but there are downsides, much like how 1e Spell Tolerance worked. 2e Spell Control doesn't really resemble 1e Spell Control in that sense.<br /> <br /> (That being said, I like 2e Spell Control a lot better than 1e Spell Tolerance, and I doubt we'll see many Mages blowing 4+ points of Reach past their Spell Control considering the sheer amount and level of badness that could result in).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1909,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1909-juhn","user":"Juhn","date":". 01-26-2016, 07:23 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1909-juhn","name":"Juhn","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"302"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-19T06:33:32-07:00","id":989848,"title":"","content":"Found this tier list thread, and noticed it's been almost a year since it's been updated. With at least 3 new books out now since this was created, how does the tier list for supernaturals look now. <br /> <br /> (Ps. I know it's comparing apples to oranges, I'm just curious on how the tiers would look now. I know everyone's overpowered in their own way, that's what made me interested in this game in the first place.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12556-salsacookies","name":"Salsacookies","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"29"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-19T09:46:41-07:00","id":989922,"title":"","content":"I don't generally think tiers are very useful in ChroD. As other people have said, each game is built with a different template for success. Demon is about espionage, Werewolf about the hunt, Vampire about social politics. This lends them all unique standards for &quot;success&quot; in the same way that default success standards might be combat in D&amp;D, investigation and psychological steeliness in Call of Cthulhu, and wetworks in Shadowrun. You wouldn't rank CoC characters according to who's best at slaying dragons or D&amp;D characters according to who's best at maintaining their sanity (except perhaps in a Ravenloft game).<br /> <br /> But since we've already been going strong with the D&amp;D comparison, here's a potential thought exercise. If default, middle-of-the-road characters from each of the core books were playing a gam of Dungeons and Dragons, what class would they represent?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8492-dxanders","name":"dxanders","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"378"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-19T10:28:43-07:00","id":989947,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>dxanders</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/810975-power-tiers-in-2e?p=989922#post989922\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't generally think tiers are very useful in ChroD. As other people have said, each game is built with a different template for success. Demon is about espionage, Werewolf about the hunt, Vampire about social politics. This lends them all unique standards for &quot;success&quot; in the same way that default success standards might be combat in D&amp;D, investigation and psychological steeliness in Call of Cthulhu, and wetworks in Shadowrun. You wouldn't rank CoC characters according to who's best at slaying dragons or D&amp;D characters according to who's best at maintaining their sanity (except perhaps in a Ravenloft game).<br /> <br /> But since we've already been going strong with the D&amp;D comparison, here's a potential thought exercise. If default, middle-of-the-road characters from each of the core books were playing a gam of Dungeons and Dragons, what class would they represent?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Obviously Mage is the Wizard. Pretty much that in every reasonable sense of the word. Needs preptime, often times a glass canon without buffing and so on.<br /> <br /> Werewolf I think obviously is a strange hybrid class of Barbarian and Ranger. Favored enemy, rage, lots of health for tanking, not exactly the best armor.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/607039-homebrew-mechs-walkers-ect\" target=\"_blank\">Mechs:</a> Because even the Chronicles of Darkness needs robot fights.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/813387-darkframe-a-far-future-crossover-setting\" target=\"_blank\">DarkFrame</a>: Crossover setting that puts Chronicles of Darkness in the far future that is Warframe.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless\" target=\"_blank\">Monarch: The Endless</a> You are an alien ruler, charged with maintaining a people who you shape to suit your needs.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7015-almarck","name":"Almarck","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-19T11:05:42-07:00","id":989968,"title":"","content":"Yeah, I was thinking ranger-druid but barbarian makes more sense for a middle-of-the-road werewolf. A lot of the games depth comes from out of combat.<br /> <br /> Tempted to say rogue for vampire, if only for the darkness stuff. There's a lot of alternate-rogue types that would fit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-19T11:38:57-07:00","id":989985,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>dxanders</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/810975-power-tiers-in-2e?p=989922#post989922\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But since we've already been going strong with the D&amp;D comparison, here's a potential thought exercise. If default, middle-of-the-road characters from each of the core books were playing a gam of Dungeons and Dragons, what class would they represent?</div> </div> </div> </div>It's multiple degrees removed from DnD, but I'm fond of describing Nightmare-oriented Beasts as Blue Mages.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-19T12:11:03-07:00","id":990012,"title":"","content":"I'll assume our characters are up with the times and playing 5E, and I'll also assume this is about what characters would choose to play rather than what they'd adapt directly into. Avoiding dual-classing while I'm at it.<br /> <br /> <b>Vampire:</b> Sorcerer? I'm not sure what would best fit them, but that would give them a nice spread of activate-at-will powers that simulate their breadth of disciplines.<br /> <b>Werewolf: </b>Ranger, what with the capacity to hunt and harry prey and take advantage of the environment around them to their benefit. Barbarian would also be appealing, I think.<br /> <b>Mage: </b>Wizard. Access to all the spells you could ever want, but you have to prepare in advance for the challenges ahead.<br /> <b>Changeling: </b>Bard. Buff your pals, disadvantage your opponents with song, dance, and poetry!<br /> <b>Mummy: </b>Warlock. Limitless power granted to you by a profane entity.<br /> <b>Hunter: </b>Paladin or cleric for tier three hunters. Plain jane warrior for the first two tiers.<br /> <b>Demon: </b>Thief, dashing to an assassin specialization as quick as their feet will carry them there.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8492-dxanders","name":"dxanders","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"378"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-19T12:21:00-07:00","id":990019,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/810975-power-tiers-in-2e?p=989968#post989968\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, I was thinking ranger-druid but barbarian makes more sense for a middle-of-the-road werewolf. A lot of the games depth comes from out of combat.</div> </div> </div> </div>Druid fits too though, because of the spirit magic. Using 4E's power source &amp; combat role model, Werewolves are undoubtedly Primal power source. Defender is probably their primary role, and they can be secondary Strikers or Leaders, depending on build choices.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/810975-power-tiers-in-2e?p=989968#post989968\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Tempted to say rogue for vampire, if only for the darkness stuff. There's a lot of alternate-rogue types that would fit.</div> </div> </div> </div>Shadow power source, Charisma-based Striker. Maybe some secondary Controller aspects, but mostly they're there to be the party face and to do heavy single-target damage when they can get a surprise round. Basically Assassins.<br /> <br /> Changelings are pretty obviously Bards. Arcane power source, Charisma-based Controller/Leaders (either can be primary and the other is secondary).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-19T12:23:30-07:00","id":990021,"title":"","content":"Didn't fourth edition offer Vampire as a class?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-19T13:18:12-07:00","id":990064,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/810975-power-tiers-in-2e?p=990021#post990021\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Didn't fourth edition offer Vampire as a class?</div> </div> </div> </div>It did, but they were terrible.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-19T13:28:23-07:00","id":990070,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/810975-power-tiers-in-2e?p=990021#post990021\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Didn't fourth edition offer Vampire as a class?</div> </div> </div> </div>Terrible OP, or UP?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12556-salsacookies","name":"Salsacookies","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"29"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-19T13:45:15-07:00","id":990077,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Salsacookies</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/810975-power-tiers-in-2e?p=990070#post990070\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Terrible OP, or UP?</div> </div> </div> </div>UP. Their damage output was significantly behind the curve for their combat role (Striker) and they didn't really get anything to compensate, except some weak hp-leaching powers. If you <i>really</i> wanted to play one, your best bet was to use the Hybrid Class rules and mash them up with a better Striker.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-22T06:00:22-07:00","id":991356,"title":"","content":"Harvesting Emotions can cost a mortal 1 willpower as it slightly weakens the intensity of the emotion.<br /> <br /> Now Reaping, which is the new trick for gaining Glamour for Changelings in 2e, is far nastier.<br /> <br /> Harvesting emotions, you just feed off the glamour released into the air like vapour around your target.<br /> <br /> With Reaper you feed on the source of the emotions directly, which gives them a nasty condition, which stops them from being able to regain will power and other effects (so its really nasty against Hunters).<br /> <br /> Reaping has a cost to the Changeling, 1 Clarity, although there is a contract called terrible harvest that allows the Changeling to Reap 1 character per turn, but only pay 1 clarity.<br /> <br /> Changelings got a big boost in 2e so they can play with the big boys/girls now.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-22T06:25:14-07:00","id":991365,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>dxanders</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/810975-power-tiers-in-2e?p=989922#post989922\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But since we've already been going strong with the D&amp;D comparison, here's a potential thought exercise. If default, middle-of-the-road characters from each of the core books were playing a gam of Dungeons and Dragons, what class would they represent?</div> </div> </div> </div> Vampire = necrotic cleric, fallen paladin or dread necromancer<br /> Werewolf = druid/ranger/barbarian, depending on style<br /> Mage = wizard/sorcerer<br /> Promethean = alchemist/artificer<br /> Changeling = bard<br /> Hunter = Fighter (honorable mention to eldritch knights)<br /> Geist = cleric<br /> Demon = rogue/assassin/arcane trickster/etc<br /> Beast = warlock / summoner<br /> Deviant = spellscar / dragonmark scion?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}